(                              samples must be tested within four hours.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Activated Partial Thromboplastin time \(aPTT\) may be performed on the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              same collection tube as Prothrombin Time and Fibrinogen.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The current lot of aPTT reagent is consistent with previous lots.  The ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mean of the reference range with this reagent is 27 seconds; the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              reference range is 23-31 seconds.  The mean of the published ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              therapeutic range for heparinization of 1.5-2.5 times the mean of the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              reference range \(27\) yields values of 40-67 seconds with this reagent. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Based on our studies of heparin responsiveness, this is a reasonable ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              target range to use with this reagent when treating uncomplicated ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              venous thromboembolism. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                        See:  <br />Prothrombin Time, Plasma  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
