(Adrenocorticotropic Hormone) Tj
/F00 8 Tf
0.0000 Tw
( ) Tj
/F10 8 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 760.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                  Laboratory  Chemistry  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 750.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                  Order Code  ACTH  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 741.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    CPT Code  82024  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 731.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(           Collection Medium  <table> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 712.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <td align=center></td></tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 702.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 693.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <td width="110" valign="top" align="center">Pink top tube</td> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </table> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
( Alternate Collection Media:  Lavender top tube 3 mL \(EDTA\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  3 mL whole blood in pink tube or TWO microtainers.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(         Rejection Criteria:  Due to limited stability, add-on orders for ACTH are not accepted. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Samples that have gone through a freeze-thaw cycle are also not ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              acceptable.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  <u>Serum/Plasma Normal Range</u> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <pre>1 week - 9 years:    5-46 pg/mL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              10-18 years:         6-55 pg/mL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              19 years and older:  7-63 pg/mL</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a General Lab or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Adrenocorticotropic hormone \(ACTH\) or corticotropin is a peptide ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hormone consisting of 39 amino acids. It is produced in the anterior ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              pituitary of the brain as part of the precursor molecule pro- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              opiomelanocortin \(POMC\).  Tissue-specific cleavage results in ACTH and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              a range of related peptides.<sup>2,3</sup>  ACTH stimulates formation ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and secretion of glucocorticoids \(especially cortisol\) by the adrenal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cortex. The glucocorticoid production is regulated by various ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              factors.<sup>4</sup> After stimulation \(e.g. by physical effort or by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the internal body clock\), the hypothalamus secretes CRH \(corticotropin ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              releasing hormone\). CRH acts on the pituitary, which in turn ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              synthesizes and secretes ACTH.  Finally, ACTH stimulates secretion of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the glucocorticoids by the adrenals.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              High concentrations of glucocorticoids in the blood inhibit secretion ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of CRH and ACTH via a negative feedback mechanism. ACTH concentrations ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              show a diurnal variation with high levels in the morning and low levels ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in the evening. Therefore, as with cortisol, it is important to know ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the collection time of the plasma sample for interpretation of the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              results. Plasma ACTH measurements are useful in the differential ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              diagnosis of pituitary Cushing's disease \(ACTH hypersecretion\), ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              autonomous ACTH-producing pituitary tumors, hypopituitarism with ACTH ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              deficiency and ectopic ACTH syndrome.<sup>5,6</sup> In addition to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cortisol measurements, ACTH determinations can be used together with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              functional or stimulation tests to diagnose the origin of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              glucocorticoid overproduction. Similarly, ACTH measurements can be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              employed to facilitate differential diagnosis of adrenocortical ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              insufficiency \(Addison's disease\). ACTH not produced by the pituitary ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              gland is known as ectopic ACTH.  This is often associated with small ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cell carcinoma of the lung. In rare cases ectopic ACTH can be caused by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              thymic tumors, pancreatic adenocarcinomas, or bronchial ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              carcinoids.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The Roche Diagnostics Elecsys ACTH assay employs two monoclonal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              antibodies specific for ACTH \(9-12\) and for the C-terminal region \(ACTH ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              36-39\). Due to common antigenic structure, the antibodies recognize ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              intact biologically active ACTH 1-39 and the ACTH precursors POMC and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              pro-ACTH.<sup>3</sup><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <pre><u>References</u>: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1. Reisch N, Reincke M, Bindlingmaier M.  Preanalytical stability of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              adrenocorticotropic hormone depends on time centrifugation rather than ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              temperature.  Clin Chem 2007;53:358-359. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              2. Cone RD. Anatomy and regulation of the central melanocortin system. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Nature Neurosci 2005;8:571-578. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              3. Talbot JA, Kane JW, White A. Analytical and clinical aspects of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              adrenocorticotrophin determination. Ann Clin Biochem 2003;40:453-471. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              4. Jacobson L. Hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenocortical axis regulation. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 78.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Endocrinol Metab Clin North Am 2005;34:271-292. ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
