stream
72 792 m
523 792 l
S
BT
0 G
1 i 0 J 0 j 0.1 w 10 M []0 d
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 797 Tm
(Pathology Laboratory Handbook) Tj
1 0 0 1 523 797 Tm
() Tj
/F10 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 758.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre><strong>Useful for:</strong> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 734.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                Diagnosis and treatment of liver, bone, intestinal, and parathyroid ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                diseases ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                Determining the tissue source of increased alkaline phosphatase \(ALP\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 686.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                activity in serum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                Differentiating between liver and bone sources of elevated ALP ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 638.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Alkaline phosphatase \(ALP\) is present in a number of tissues including ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              liver, bone, intestine, and placenta. The activity of ALP found in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 614.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              serum is a composite of isoenzymes from those sites and, in some ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              circumstances, placental or Regan isoenzymes. Serum ALP is of interest ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 590.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in the diagnosis of 2 main groups of conditions-hepatobiliary disease ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and bone disease associated with increased osteoblastic activity. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 554.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              A rise in ALP activity occurs with all forms of cholestasis, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 542.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              particularly with obstructive jaundice. The response of the liver to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              any form of biliary tree obstruction is to synthesize more ALP. The ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 518.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              main site of new enzyme synthesis is the hepatocytes adjacent to the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 506.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              biliary canaliculi. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ALP also is elevated in disorders of the skeletal system that involve ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 470.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              osteoblast hyperactivity and bone remodeling, such as Paget's disease ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 458.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              rickets and osteomalacia, fractures, and malignant tumors. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Moderate elevation of ALP may be seen in other disorders such as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 422.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Hodgkin's disease, congestive heart failure, ulcerative colitis, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 410.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              regional enteritis, and intra-abdominal bacterial infections. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  <strong>Total Alkaline Phosphatase \(ALP\)</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 374.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ALP cleaves p-nitrophenyl phosphate in the presence of magnesium ion to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 362.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              yield phosphate and p-nitrophenol. The rate of p-nitrophenol formation ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 350.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              is directly proportional to the ALP activity and is determined ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              photometrically at 450 nm.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 326.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 314.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <strong>ALP Isoenzymes</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 302.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Serum samples are electrophoresed through alkaline buffered \(pH 9.1\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              agarose gels. Almost all ALP isoenzymes can be separated by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 278.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              electrophoresis according to their charge difference. However, because ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 266.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the electrophoretic mobilities of the liver and bone isoenzymes are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 254.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              quite similar, a modification is required for separation. The Sebia ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              system utilizes differences between liver and bone isoenzyme sialation ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 230.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in order to achieve separation. Each sample is applied to the agarose ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 218.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              gel in duplicate. One sample is passed through wheat germ lectin \(wheat ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 206.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              germ agglutin [WGA]\) and is deposited anodally from the point of sample ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              application. The bone isoenzyme, which is rich in sialic acids, reacts ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 182.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with WGA and precipitates adjacent to the lectin application point. The ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 170.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              separated isoenzymes are visualized using a specific chromogenic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 158.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              substrate, 5-bromo-4-chloro-3-indolyl phosphate/nitro blue tetrazolium ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in aminomethyl propanol \(AMP\) buffer, pH 10.0. The dried gels are read ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 134.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              on a densitometer for the quantification of tissue isoforms.   ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 122.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  4 days upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 110.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(            Testing Schedule  Alkaline Phosphatase: Monday through Sunday; Continuously<br/> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Alkaline Phosphatase Isoenzymes: Monday through Friday  ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(24) Tj
