1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Adjunct in the diagnosis of pituitary tumors<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              As part of the follow-up of treated pituitary tumor patients<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Differential diagnosis of thyrotropin-secreting pituitary tumor versus ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              thyroid hormone resistance<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Differential diagnosis of constitutional delay of puberty versus ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hypogonadotrophic hypogonadism<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <u>Cautions</u>:<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              False-positive elevations in serum free alpha-subunit levels may be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              seen in some women if blood specimens are drawn within 24 hours of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ovulation.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Patients with end-stage renal failure may have serum free alpha-subunit ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              concentrations of up to 6-times the upper limit of reference ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              range.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Elevated alpha-subunit results on patients with elevated thyrotropin ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(TSH\) should be interpreted with caution due to TSH cross-reactivity ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with the assay.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Assisted reproduction involving ovarian hyperstimulation or in vitro ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              fertilization may be associated with the elevation in serum free alpha- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              subunit levels.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pregnancy is associated with very substantial, physiological elevations ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in serum free alpha-subunit levels, paralleling chorionic gonadotropin ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(hCG\) secretion. This test should not be ordered on pregnant ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              patients.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Thyrotropin-releasing hormone \(TRH\) and gonadotropin releasing hormone ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(GnRH\) testing are not performed in the laboratory, but in specialized ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              clinical testing units under the supervision of a physician.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
