1 0 0 1 72 797 Tm
(Pathology Laboratory Handbook) Tj
1 0 0 1 523 797 Tm
() Tj
/F00 8 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 770.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
() Tj
/F01 8 Tf
0.0000 Tw
(Anaerobic Culture) Tj
/F00 8 Tf
0.0000 Tw
( ) Tj
/F10 8 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 760.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                  Laboratory  Microbiology  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 750.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(           Collection Medium  Sterile container  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 741.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Clinical Microbiology Laboratory or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 731.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Tissue or aspirates are preferred rather than swabs. Fluid collections ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 712.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              should be aspirated through disinfected tissue or skin. For superficial ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 702.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ulcers, collect material from below the surface \(after surface ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 693.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              debridement or use a needle and syringe\). Submit specimens using ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              anaerobic transport media: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 664.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              a. Anaerobic transport vial \(fluid specimen, 59546\): Cleanse rubber ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              stopper with alcohol; allow to dry 1 min before inoculation; push ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              needle through septum and inject specimen on top of agar. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              b. Anaerobic jar \(tissue specimen, 59547\). Place sample on top of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              agar.  Keep jar upright to maintain atmosphere in jar. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              c. A sterile container \(37778\) may be used for tissue if transported to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the microbiology lab immediately \(add drops of sterile saline to keep ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              small pieces of tissue moist\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              d. Copan Liquid Amies Elution Swab \(ESwab\) \(74541\) - swab specimens are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              suboptimal, aspirate preferred but will be accepted if no other sample ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              can be obtained. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              e. Deliver all specimens to the laboratory immediately after  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              collection. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              f. Anaerobic flora is prevalent on mucosal surfaces of the oral cavity, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              upper respiratory, gastrointestinal, and genital tracts; specimens ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              collected from these sites should not ordinarily be cultured for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              anaerobic bacteria. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The following is a list of specimens that are likely to be contaminated ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with anaerobic normal flora and are NOT routinely accepted for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              anaerobic culture. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Throat or nasopharyngeal swabs ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Gingival or other intraoral surface swabs ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Expectorated sputum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Sputum obtained by nasotracheal or endotracheal suction ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Bronchial washings ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
