(                     Minimum  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Adult - 5 mL; red top tube ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pediatric - 2 mL; red top tube</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Negative: <20 units ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Equivocal: 20-24 units ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Positive: >25 units</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Immunopathology or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The results will be obtained with the INOVA QUANTA Lite&#0153; ELISA. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Assay values obtained with different manufacturers' methods may not be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              used interchangeably. The magnitude of the reported antibody levels can ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              not be correlated to an endpoint titer. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ASCA testing may be clinically useful in the evaluation of suspected ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              inflammatory bowel disease, including Crohn's disease and ulcerative ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              colitis \(UC\). ASCA is significantly more prevalent in Crohn's disease ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              than in UC or in healthy individuals. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Published studies of Crohn's disease have reported IgG ASCA test ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              sensitivity for CD is about 74% while IgA ASCA is about 49% sensitive. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              About 25% of CD patients are repeatably negative for ASCA, therefore a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              negative result does not rule out CD. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The best specificity for CD is obtained when both IgG and IgA ASCA's ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              are positive. There are published reports of 95-100% specificity with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              dual IgG and IgA positivity. Our own disease control testing \(patients ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with a variety of GI and liver diseases\) revealed 85% specificity with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              false positives in 1 patient with Mycobacterial granulomatous ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hepatitis, 1 patient with alcoholic hepatitis and 1 patient with acute ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              colitis, probably UC.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay Test \(ELISA\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  1 week  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(            Testing Schedule  Weekly  ) Tj
