0.0000 Tw
(                              <td align=center><a href="javascript:larger_tube\('24.jpg'\)"></a></td></tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 702.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 693.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <td width="110" valign="top" align="center">CSF container</td> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </table> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  1.0 mL spinal fluid from collection vial #2.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  Normal: <1.5 ng/mL<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Elevated: > or =1.5 ng/mL; compatible with, but not diagnostic of, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  The 14-3-3 proteins are a group of highly conserved proteins composed ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of several isoforms that are involved in the regulation of protein ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              phosphorylation and mitogen-activated protein kinase pathways. They ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              exist in vivo as dimers of the various isoforms with apparent molecular ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mass of 30 kDa on sodium dodecyl sulfate polyacrylamide gel ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              electrophoresis and 60 kDa on gel chromatography. Sequence homology ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              among the various isoforms ranges from 22% to100%. The beta, gamma, and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              theta isoforms are found in tissues of the nervous system.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Detectable 14-3-3 protein in the cerebrospinal fluid \(CSF\) is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              indicative of substantial, relatively rapid neuronal destruction. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Increased CSF concentrations of 14-3-3 proteins have been described in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              patients with various forms of Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease \(CJD\), some ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              other rapidly progressive dementias, and a large range of other ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              vascular, inflammatory, neoplastic, and metabolic central nervous ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              system \(CNS\) disorders, which can be associated with significant and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              rapid neuronal destruction. <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The main clinical use of 14-3-3 measurements is in the differential ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              diagnosis of dementia, in particular to distinguish CJD and its ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              variants from other dementias. The most common forms of dementia ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(progressive multiinfarct dementia and Alzheimer disease\) are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              uncommonly associated with elevated CSF levels of 14-3-3, presumably ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              because of their slow pace of progression. <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              CJD is an incurable neurodegenerative disease caused by accumulation of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              self-catalytically malfolded endogenous prion proteins in the CNS. Its ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cause is most commonly sporadic, but it can be inherited \(mutations ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              that predispose to malfolding\) or acquired \(iatrogenic transmission by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              infected human tissues or tissue extracts or surgical procedures, or by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ingestion of some animal products that contain malfolded prion ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              proteins\). <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The diagnosis of CJD is highly complex and involves clinical history ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and neurologic examination, electroencephalographs \(EEG\), magnetic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              resonance imaging \(MRI\), and exclusion of other possible causes of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              dementia, in addition to CSF examination. Several, slightly different ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              scoring systems are in use to integrate these parameters into a final ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              diagnosis of possible, probable, or definite CJD. The most widely ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              accepted of these scoring systems is the WHO set of diagnostic criteria ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              for sporadic CJD from 1998.<br/> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Hemolyzed specimens will be rejected. Hemolysis causes falsely-elevated ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              14-3-3 results. The 14-3-3 concentrations in 82 visibly blood-tinged ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cerebrospinal fluid \(CSF\) specimens were up to 281 ng/mL, with 74 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              specimens \(90.2%\) showing levels above the cutoff. <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              In addition, specimens may be determined to be unsuitable for testing ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              if any of the following conditions are observed:\(1,2\) <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Macroscopically hemorrhagi<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Xanthochromic<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -RBC counts >500 cells per mcL<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -WBC counts >10 cells per mcL<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 78.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Regardless of the method used, measurement of 14-3-3 protein in CSF ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 69.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              should not be relied upon exclusively to establish the diagnosis of ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(Updated:Mon Aug 26 14:13:27 2013) Tj
1 0 0 1 511.88 37 Tm
(59) Tj
