(                              Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease \(CJD\). Increased concentrations of 14-3-3 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              protein in CSF have been described in a variety of central nervous ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 734.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              system \(CNS\) diseases other than CJD that are associated with relative ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              rapid \(days to months, rather than months to years\) destruction of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 710.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              significant amounts of CNS neuronal tissue. Published examples include: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              infectious encephalitides, transverse myelitis, stroke, intracerebral ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 686.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and subarachnoid hemorrhage, rapidly progressive vascular dementia, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              various metabolic and anoxic encephalopathies, severe acute CNS ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              episodes of multiple sclerosis, cerebral vasculitides and angiopathies, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mitochondrial encephalomyelopathies, CNS storage diseases, widespread ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 638.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              or rapidly growing primary or secondary CNS and leptomeningeal tumors, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and, rarely, Alzheimer disease and other primary dementias. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
