BT
0 G
1 i 0 J 0 j 0.1 w 10 M []0 d
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 797 Tm
(Pathology Laboratory Handbook) Tj
1 0 0 1 523 797 Tm
() Tj
/F10 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 758.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       alcohol swabs. Allow septum to dry for 1 min before ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       inoculating. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 734.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    4\) Draw 20 mL of blood and inoculate each bottle with 10 mL of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       blood.  Do not vent or overfill bottles. Adding low \(<8 mL\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 710.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       or high \(>10 mL\) volumes may adversely affect the recovery of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       organisms.  Transport time <2 h. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 686.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    5\) For adults with a suspected bloodstream infection \(BSI\), ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       collect two initial sets of blood cultures sequentially from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       separate phlebotomy procedures followed by a third set at 4-6 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       hour intervals \(will detect >98% of BSIs\). A single set of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 638.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       blood cultures to detect BSIs in adults is inadequate \(only ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       73% sensitivity\); two sets of blood cultures will allow ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 614.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       detection of 87.7-89.7% of BSI episodes.  \(J Clin Microbiol ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       2007;45:3546\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 590.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    6\) If patient is allergic to chlorhexidine, prep site with a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       povidone iodine swab stick \(907172\) applied in concentric ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 566.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       circles \(start at center\). Allow to dry at least 1 min before ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 554.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       venipuncture. If patient is allergic to iodine, cleanse site ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 542.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       with 70% alcohol for 60 sec. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 b. <u>Pediatric</u> - Apart from NICU patients, the minimum volume ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 518.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    drawn should be 1 mL per year of age per blood culture set. This ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 506.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    volume should be split between an aerobic and anaerobic bottle. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 494.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    See pediatric blood culture order for more detail. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 470.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              D. <u>Bone marrow aspirate</u> - Prepare puncture site as for surgical ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 458.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 incision.  Inoculate blood culture bottle \(924171\) or Isolator ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 446.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 \(lysis centrifugation\) tube \(922848\).  Transport time <2 hours. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 Routine bacterial culture of bone marrow is rarely useful. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 410.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              E. <u>Burn</u> - Clean and debride burn. Place tissue in sterile screw- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 398.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 cap container \(37778\). Transfer aspirates to a sterile container. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 These are processed for aerobic culture only. Quantitative culture ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 374.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 may or may not be valuable. A 3 to 4 mm punch biopsy specimen is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 362.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 optimum when quantitative cultures are ordered. Cultures of surface ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 350.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 samples can be misleading. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 326.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              F. <u>Catheter Tips</u> - Only intravascular catheter tips from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 314.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 pediatric patients and SICU patients are routinely accepted for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 302.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 culture. Send 5 cm of distal tip in sterile screw-cap container ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 \(37778\). Transport time is &#8804;15 min.  Foley catheters are not ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 278.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 accepted for culture since growth represents distal urethral flora. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 254.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              G. <u>Cerebrospinal Fluid \(CSF\)</u> - Aseptically collect CSF from a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 lumbar puncture into sterile tubes \(907131\). Send second tube ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 230.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 \(&#8805;3 mL\) to the Microbiology Laboratory.  Transport time ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 218.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 &#8804;15 min. Cerebrospinal fluid for bacterial culture should ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 206.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 never be refrigerated. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 182.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              H. <u>Decubitus ulcer</u> - A swab is not the specimen of choice. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 170.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 Cleanse surface with sterile saline. Submit tissue or aspirate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 158.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 inflammatory material from the base of the ulcer in a sterile tube ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 or anaerobic system.  Transport time is &#8804;2 hours. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 122.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              I. <u>Ear</u> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 110.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 a. <u>Inner ear</u> - Tympanocentesis should be reserved for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    complicated, recurrent, or chronic persistent otitis media. For ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 86.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    intact eardrum, clean ear canal with soap solution and collect ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 74.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    fluid via syringe aspiration. Submit in sterile container. For ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
