1 0 0 1 102.0 758.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    ruptured eardrum, collect fluid on flexible shaft swab via an ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    auditory speculum.  Transport time <2 hours. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 734.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 b. <u>Outer ear</u> - Use moistened swab to remove any debris or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    crust from ear canal. Obtain sample by firmly rotating swab in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 710.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    outer canal. For otitis externa, vigorous swabbing is required - ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    surface swabbing may miss streptococcal cellulitis. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              J. <u>Eye</u> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 a. <u>Conjunctiva</u> - Sample each eye with separate swabs ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    \(premoistened with sterile saline\) by rolling over conjunctiva. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 638.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    When only one eye is infected, sampling both can help distinguish ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    indigenous microflora from true pathogens. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 614.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 b. <u>Corneal scrapings</u> - Collected by ophthalmologist. Using ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    sterile spatula, scrape ulcers and lesions; inoculate scraping ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 590.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    directly onto media \(BHI with 10% sheep blood, chocolate, and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    inhibitory mold agar\). Prepare 2 smears by rubbing material onto ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 566.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    1-2 cm area of slide. Transport time &#8804;15 min. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 554.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 c. <u>Vitreous fluid</u> - Prepare eye for needle aspiration of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 542.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    fluid. Transfer fluid to sterile tube. Transport time ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    &#8804;15 min. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 506.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              K. <u>Feces</u> - see stool. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              L. <u>Fistula</u> - see abscess. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 458.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              M. <u>Fluids</u> - see sterile body fluids. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              N. <u>Genital</u> - Cultures for <em>Neisseria gonorrhoeae</em> should ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 422.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 be collected using a Copan Liquid amies Elution Swab \(ESwab\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 410.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 Transport to laboratory immediately. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 398.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 a. <u>Endocervical</u> - Remove cervical mucus with swab and  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              discard. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 374.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    Insert a second swab into endocervical canal and rotate against ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 362.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    walls. Allow time for organisms to absorb onto the swab surface. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 350.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 b. <u>Urethral</u> - Collect urethral specimens at least 1 h after ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    patient has urinated. Insert small swab 2-4 cm into urethral ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 326.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    lumen, rotate, leave for 2s to facilitate absorption. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 302.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              O. <u>Pilonidal cyst</u> - see abscess. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 278.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              P. <u>Respiratory, lower</u> - Transport time is &#8804;2 hours. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 266.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 a. <u>Bronchoalveolar lavage or brush, endotracheal aspirate</u> - ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 254.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    Collect fluid in a sputum trap \(907093\); transfer to leak-proof ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    container \(37778\) for transport in pneumatic tube system\); place ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 230.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    brush in sterile container with 1 mL saline. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 218.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 b. <u>Sputum, expectorated</u> - Patient should rinse mouth and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 206.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    gargle with water prior to collection; instruct patient to cough ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    deeply.  Collect specimens in sterile transport containers ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 182.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    \(37778\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 170.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 c. <u>Sputum, induced</u> - Have patient brush gums and teeth, then ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 158.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    rinse mouth thoroughly with water.  Using a nebulizer, have the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    patient inhale 20-30 mL of 3 to 10% sterile saline.  Collect ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 134.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    sputum in sterile container. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 122.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 d. <u>If Nocardia is suspected</u>, culture for Nocardia should be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 110.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    requested as an add-on test as standard culture is inadequate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    for its recovery. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 74.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Q. <u>Respiratory, upper</u> - Transport time &#8804;2 hours. ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
