1 0 0 1 72 797 Tm
(Pathology Laboratory Handbook) Tj
1 0 0 1 523 797 Tm
() Tj
/F10 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 758.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 a. <u>Oral</u> - remove oral secretions and debris from surface of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    lesion with a swab.  Use a second swab to vigorously sample ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 734.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    lesion, avoiding normal tissue.  Superficial swab specimens ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    should not be submitted.  Tissue or needle aspirates are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 710.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    preferred. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 b. <u>Nasal swabs \(R/O SAPCR\)</u> - Insert a sterile swab \(use Copan ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 686.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    dual swab 26200\) into the nose until resistance is met at the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    level of the turbinates \(approximately 1-2 cm into one nostril\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    Rotate the swab against the nasal mucosa for 3 sec.  Apply slight ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    pressure with a finger on the outside of the nose to ensure good ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 638.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    contact between swab and inside of nose. Using the same swab, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    repeat for the other nostril. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 614.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 c. <u>Sinus aspirates</u> - Aspirate with needle and syringe. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    Cleanse rubber stopper of anaerobic transport  vial \(59546\) with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 590.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    alcohol; push needle through septum and inject specimen on top of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    agar. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 566.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 d. <u>Throat</u> - Routine throat cultures will be processed only ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 554.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    for growth of &#946;-hemolytic <em>Streptococcus</em> species. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 542.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    Do not obtain throat samples if epiglottis is inflamed, as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    sampling may cause serious respiratory obstruction.  Sample the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 518.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    posterior pharynx, tonsils, and inflamed areas with a Copan ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 506.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    Liquid Amies Elution Swab \(ESwab\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              R. <u>Sterile body fluids</u> \(other than CSF\) - ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 470.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 a. Transport fluid to laboratory in sterile, leak-proof container ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 458.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    \(BD Vacutainer, no additive, yellow top, 924044\) or anaerobic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 446.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    transport vial \(Vial, 59546\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 b. Cleanse rubber septum of container with 70% alcohol. Allow septum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 422.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    to dry for 1 min before inoculating. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 410.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 c. Disinfect overlying skin with iodine or chlorhexidine ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 398.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    preparation.  Obtain specimen with needle and syringe. Push ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    needle through septum of transport container and inject fluid. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 374.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 d. Amniotic and culdocentesis fluids should always be transported in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 362.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    an anaerobic transport vial \(59546\). Agar in anaerobic vial ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 350.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    should be clear before inoculation; inject fluid on top of agar. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 e. Submit as much fluid as possible. NEVER submit a swab dipped in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 326.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    fluid. NEVER inject fluid into swab container. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 314.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 f. One aerobic blood culture bottle \(924171\) inoculated at bedside ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 302.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    \(up to 10 mL\) is highly recommended provided adequate sample is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    available. If blood culture bottle is inoculated, submit separate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 278.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    aliquot in anaerobic transport vial \(59546\) or sterile container ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 266.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    \(924044\) for preparation of cytocentrifuged Gram stain and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 254.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    inoculation of solid media \(allows quantitation, aids in culture ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    interpretation\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 230.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 g. Transport time &#8804;15 min, room temperature. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 206.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              S. <u>Stool</u> - Stools submitted on patients admitted for >3 days ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 will be rejected without prior preapproval \(pager 4903 weekdays; ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 182.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 pager 3404 evenings and weekends\). Submit 10-20 g in sterile ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 170.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 container. Transport time is &#8804;1 hour. Refrigerate if transport ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 158.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 is delayed. Stools are cultured to isolate bacterial causative ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 agents of diarrheal illness; <em>Salmonella, Shigella,</em> and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 134.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 <em>Campylobacter</em>. Routine stool culture includes EIA ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 122.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 for Shiga toxin from <em>E. coli</em>. Cultures for Yersinia are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 110.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 performed by special request. Stools for <em>C. difficile</em> toxin ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 detection must be transported to the laboratory immediately or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 86.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 refrigerated if transport is delayed. Surveillance cultures may be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 74.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 ordered on Bone Marrow transplant and other immunocompromised ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(78) Tj
1 0 0 1 355.18 37 Tm
(Updated:Mon Aug 26 14:13:27 2013) Tj
