() Tj
1 0 0 1 367.98 797 Tm
(Pathology Laboratory Handbook) Tj
/F10 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 758.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 patients to detect overgrowth of normal flora by <em>Staph ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 aureus</em>, yeast or a gram negative bacillus. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              T. <u>Tissue</u> - Submit in anaerobic collection jar \(59547\) or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 710.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 sterile screw-cap container \(37778\); add drops of sterile saline to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 keep small pieces of tissue moist.  Transport time &#8804;15 min. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              U. <u>Urine</u> - Collect 20 mL of urine in a sterile specimen ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 container \(37778\). Transfer urine to a Boricon urine transport ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 container. Transport to the microbiology laboratory. If unable to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 638.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 collect 20 mL of urine, collect in sterile specimen container ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 \(37778\) and transport urine specimens to the Microbiology ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 614.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 Laboratory or refrigerate <strong>within 30 minutes</strong>. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 Refrigerated specimens should be delivered to the lab as soon as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 590.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 possible, and may be rejected if not received within 24 hours of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 collection. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 566.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 a. <u>Midstream clean catch method</u>: Patients should be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 554.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    instructed to wash hands prior to collection and offered exam ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 542.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    gloves. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    1. <strong>Female</strong> patients should be instructed to sit ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 518.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       on toilet with legs apart and spread labia with one hand. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 506.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       First void in toilet and then, continuing to void, hold ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 494.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       specimen container in "midstream" to collect sample. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    2. <strong>Male</strong> patients should be instructed to retract ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 470.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       foreskin if uncircumcised. First void in toilet and then, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 458.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       continuing to void, hold specimen container in "midstream" to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 446.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                       collect sample. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 b. <u>Straight catheter</u>: Thoroughly cleanse the urethral opening ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 422.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    with soap and water. Rinse area with wet gauze pads. Aseptically ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 410.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    insert catheter into the bladder. After discarding initial 15 to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 398.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    30 mL of urine, collect 20 mL of urine for submission in a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    Boricon urine transport container. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 374.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 c. <u>Indwelling catheter</u>: Clamp catheter below port and allow ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 362.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    urine to collect in tubing. Disinfect the catheter collection ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 350.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    port with 70% alcohol. Use needle and syringe to aseptically ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    collect 20 mL freshly voided urine though catheter port. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 326.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    Transfer to Boricon urine transport container. Do not collect ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 314.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    urine from collection bag. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 302.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 d. <u>Ileal conduit</u>: Remove the external device and discard  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              urine ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 278.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    within device. Gently cleanse the stoma with 70% alcohol ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 266.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    followed by povidone-iodine swab stick \(907172\). Using sterile ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 254.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    technique, insert a double catheter into the cleansed stoma, to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    a depth beyond the fascial level, and collect the urine into a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 230.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    sterile container. Transfer to a Boricon urine transport ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 218.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    container.  Use of a double catheter helps to minimize ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 206.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                    contamination of the specimen with skin flora. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 182.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              V. <u>Wound</u> - See abscess.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 158.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                See Appendix  See Additional Information: <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Microbiology Specimen Collection and Transport<br />Normal \(Indigenous\)  ) Tj
