(                     Minimum  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Draw blood in a yellow-top \(ACD\) tube. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Preferred Minimum:  7 mL of ACD whole blood ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Absolute Minimum:  5 mL of ACD whole blood</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              TPP1: 85-326 nmol/hr/mg protein ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              PPT1: 20-93 nmol/hr/mg protein</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Useful for evaluation of patients with clinical presentations ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              suggestive of NCL and an aid in the differential diagnosis of infantile ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and late infantile NCL. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Cautions:  This assay does not detect carrier status of NCL.  Some ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              variants with an age of onset occurring in older individuals have been ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              noted. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Neuronal ceroid lipofuscinoses \(NCL\) are inherited neurodegenerative ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              disorders with an overall incidence in the United States estimated ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              at1:12,500. Clinically they are characterized by vision loss, seizures, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mental regression, behavioral changes, movement disorders, and the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              accumulation of storage material with a characteristic appearance by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              electron microscopy \(EM\). Tissue damage is selective for the nervous ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              system and many patients succumb in the first decade of life due to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              central nervous system degeneration. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The infantile NCL form is caused by deficiency of the lysosomal enzyme ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              palmitoyl-protein thioesterase 1 \(PPT1\), which cleaves a thioester ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              linkage between a fatty acid \(palmitate\) and cysteine in lipid-modified ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              proteins. It is an early onset disease characterized by psychomotor ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              degeneration, seizures, and progressive macular degeneration leading to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              blindness by the age of 2. Infantile NCL is an autosomal recessive ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              disorder with an incidence of 1:20,000 in Finland and rare elsewhere. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The late infantile form of NCL is caused by deficiency of the lysosomal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              enzyme tripeptidyl peptidase 1 \(TPP1\), which cleaves tripeptides from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the N-terminus of polypeptides. Tissue damages are especially neuronal, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              resulting from the defective degradation and consequent lysosomal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              storage of small peptides. Disease onset occurs at 2 to 4 years of age ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with death occurring around the age of 10.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Fluorometric  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
