(                              <td width="110" valign="top" align="center">BD Gold SST 5&nbsp;mL Vacutainer</td> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </table> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Adult Absolute Minimum:  0.5 mL serum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pediatric Absolute Minimum:  0.2 mL serum</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(         Rejection Criteria:  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Lipemic, icteric, or hemolyzed specimens.  Specimens that have been ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              stored at ambient temperature.  Specimens that have been stored at ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              2-8&#176;C for >5 days.  If storage longer than 5 days is needed, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              samples should be frozen at -70&#176;C. Unless indicated as stored ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              frozen, the specimen will be rejected if the draw date is >5 days from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              receipt at reference laboratory.</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Negative: Less than 60 pg/mL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Indeterminate: 60 to less than 80 pg/mL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Positive: Greater than or equal to 80 pg/mL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The Fungitell beta-D Glucan assay is indicated for presumptive ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              diagnosis of fungal infection. It should be used in conjunction with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              other diagnostic procedures. The Fungitell beta-D Glucan assay does not ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              detect certain fungal species such as the genus Cryptococcus, which ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              produces very low levels of \(1,3\)- beta-D-glucan. This assay also does ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              not detect the Zygomycetes, such as Absidia, Mucor and Rhizopus, which ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              are not known to produce \(1,3\)- beta-D-glucan.</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The Fungitell beta-D Glucan assay is indicated for the presumptive ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              diagnosis of invasive fungal disease through detection of elevated ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              levels of \(1,3\)- beta-D-glucan in serum. Normal human serum contains ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              low levels of \(1,3\)- beta-D glucan, typically 10 to 40 pg/mL, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              presumably from commensal yeasts present in the alimentary canal and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              gastrointestinal tract. However, \(1,3\)- beta-D-glucan is sloughed from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the cell walls during the life cycle of most pathogenic fungi. Thus, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              monitoring serum for evidence of elevated and rising levels of \(1,3\)- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              beta-D-glucan provides a convenient surrogate marker for invasive ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              fungal disease. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The Fungitell beta-D Glucan assay detects \(1,3\)- beta-D-glucan from the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              following pathogens:  Candida spp., Acremonium, Aspergillus spp., ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Coccidioides immitis, Fusarium spp., Histoplasma capsulatum, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Trichosporon spp., Sporothrix schenckii, Saccharomyces cerevisiae, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pneumocystis jiroveci. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The Fungitell beta-D Glucan assay does not detect certain fungal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              species such as the genus Cryptococcus, which produces very low levels ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of \(1,3\)- beta-D-glucan, nor the Zygomycetes, such as Absidia, Mucor, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and Rhizopus, which are not known to produce \(1,3\)- beta-D-glucan. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Studies indicate Blastomyces dermatitidis is usually not detected due ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              to little \(1,3\)- beta-D-glucan produced in the yeast phase.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Enzyme Immunoassay \(EIA\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
