( Alternate Collection Media:  Call laboratory for additional acceptable specimen collection containers.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  3 mL whole blood from light green top tube or 1 light green top ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              microtainer for pediatric patients.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  0.0-0.3 mEq/l  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a General Lab or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Ketosis is a common feature in acutely ill patients.  In subjects ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              suffering from starvation, acute alcohol abuse, or diabetes mellitus, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ketosis can result in severe life-threatening metabolic acidosis.  The ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              presence and degree of ketosis can be determined by measuring blood ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              levels of &#946;-hydroxybutyrate.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Ordinarily, &#946;-hydroxybutyrate is the ketoacid present in the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              greatest amount in serum.  It accounts for approximately 75% of the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ketone bodies which also include acetoacetate and acetone.  During ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              periods of ketosis, &#946;-hydroxybutyrate increases even more than the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              other two keto acids \(acetoacetate and acetone\), and has been shown to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              be a good index of ketoacidosis, including the detection of subclinical ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ketosis.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              In diabetics, the measurement of &#946;-hydroxybutyrate as well as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              blood glucose can help to assess the severity of diabetic coma and help ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              exclude hyperosmolar non-ketotic diabetic coma.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The &#946;-hydroxybutyrate assay is specific for &#946;-hydroxybutyrate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and shows no cross-reactivity with acetoacetate or acetone. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                        See:  <br />Beta-Hydroxybutyrate-Other, Body Fluid ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br />Urinalysis, Urine  ) Tj
