(                 Order Form:  A-1a Clinical Microbiology Laboratory or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  All specimens sent for malarial examination will be initially screened ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with a malarial antigen assay. This assay can rapidly identify patients ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              infected with Plasmodium falciparum at levels of 0.1% or higher, and it ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              can also identify cases of malaria caused by other species. However, it ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cannot specifically classify Plasmodium species other than P. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              falciparum. The assay has a very high negative predictive value \(>99%\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              for malaria. All specimens will continue to be Giemsa stained and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              examined microscopically by a pathologist, regardless of the antigen ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              result. One set of negative smears does not rule out malaria. If ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              clinical suspicion for malaria remains after one set of negative ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              smears, additional specimens should be submitted at 12 hour intervals ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              for the subsequent 36 hour period.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Note on requisition if a parasite infection other than malaria is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              suspected.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Please contact the Microbiology resident from 0800-1700 \(pager 4903\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with questions. After hours, contact the Clinical Pathology resident on ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              call \(pager 3404\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Lateral Flow Assay for antigen testing.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Microscopic slide examination.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  Antigen results will be available within one hour of specimen arrival,  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              24 hours a day.  Preliminary thin smear results will be available  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              within 90 minutes of specimen arrival if the specimen arrives between  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              0700-1900 or by 0930 if specimen arrives after hours.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(            Testing Schedule  Giemsa smears and Malaria antigen testing 24 hrs/day, 7 days a week,  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              including holidays.  ) Tj
