(                    CPT Code  87493  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 731.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(           Collection Medium  Sterile container  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(         Rejection Criteria:  Formed stool; specimen submitted within 10 days of positive result; ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 712.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              more than 1 specimen/week.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 702.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Clinical Microbiology Laboratory or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 693.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  This test targets toxin B gene sequences. Most pathogenic C. difficile ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              strains produce toxin A and B, but some produce only toxin B.  The ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              number of C. difficile toxin PCR test requests for a patient will ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 664.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              be limited to one per week. The higher sensitivity of PCR in comparison ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              to cell cytotoxicity and immunoassay methods supports this policy [Ann ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Intern Med 2009; 151:176].<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              It is generally recommended that C. difficile PCR be performed only for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              patients with <u>></u> 3 liquid stools within a 24 hour period. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Since C. difficile colonization rather than infection may exist, only ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              unformed stool specimens from patients with signs and symptoms of C. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              difficile infection should be tested. The significance of Clostridium ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              difficile toxin detection in infants \(<1 year old\) is uncertain because ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of the high rate of asymptomatic C. difficile carriage in this age ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              group.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Once a patient is diagnosed with C. difficile infection, therapeutic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              response should be based on clinical signs and symptoms; a "test of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cure" should not be done since patients may remain colonized with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              toxin-producing strains following recovery. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                See Appendix  See Additional Information: <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Specimens Requiring Immediate Delivery  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Polymerase Chain Reaction  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
