(                     Minimum  0.1 mL of serum  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              < or = 0.10 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              0.11 - 0.12 \(indeterminate\)</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Chronic alcoholism causes a transient change in the glycosylation ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              pattern of transferrin where the relative amounts of disialo- and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              asialotransferrin \(carbohydrate deficient transferrin [CDT]\) are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              increased over the amount of normally glycosylated ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              tetrasialotransferrin.  This recognition led to the use of CDT in serum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              as marker for chronic alcohol abuse. CDT typically normalizes within ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              several weeks of abstinence of alcohol use. However, it is important to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              recognize that there are other causes of abnormal CDT levels, which ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              include congenital disorders of glycosylation \(CDG\) and other genetic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and nongenetic causes of acute or chronic liver disease. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              CDT testing alone is not recommended for general screening for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              alcoholism; however, when combined with other methods \(ie, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              gamma-glutamyltransferase [GGT], mean corpuscular volume [MCV], patient ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              self-reporting\) clinicians can expect to identify 90% or more of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              heavily drinking patients. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              This assay has not been fully validated for the investigation of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              alcoholism. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              CDT testing alone is not recommended for general screening for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              alcoholism. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The abnormal transferrin isoform pattern in patients with chronic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              alcoholism is similar to that observed in CDGS.  However, unlike most ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              patients with CDG, the relative amount of mono-glycosylated transferrin ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              is much lower. Other conditions such as hereditary fructose ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              intolerance, galactosemia, and liver disease may result in increased ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              levels of CDT.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Affinity Chromatography/Mass Spectrometry \(MS\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  6 days upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
/F00 8 Tf
