(                    Comments  Always include Date of Birth on the request form.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Determination of urine carnitine concentration concurrently with plasma ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              concentration is recommended.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Carnitine and its esters are required for normal energy metabolism and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              serve 4 primary functions:<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Importing long-chain fatty acids into the mitochondria<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Exporting naturally-occurring short-chain acyl-CoA groups from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &nbsp;mitochondria<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Buffering the ratio of free CoA to esterified CoA<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Removing potentially toxic acyl-CoA groups from the cells and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              tissues<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Evaluation of carnitine in plasma, tissue, and urine identifies ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              patients with primary disorders of the carnitine cycle, as well as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              disturbances in carnitine levels as a result of organic acidemias and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              fatty acid oxidation disorders. In the latter disorders, acyl-CoA ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              groups accumulate and are excreted into the urine and bile as carnitine ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              derivatives, resulting in a secondary carnitine deficiency. More than ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              100 such primary and secondary disorders have been described. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Individually, the incidence of these disorders varies from <1:10,000 to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              >1:1,000,000 live births. Collectively, their incidence is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              approximately 1:1,000 live births.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Other conditions that are associated with an abnormal carnitine status ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              are neuromuscular diseases, gastrointestinal disorders, familial ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cardiomyopathy, renal tubulopathies and chronic renal failure ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(dialysis\), and prolonged treatment with steroids, antibiotics \(pivalic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              acid\), anticonvulsants \(valproic acid\), and total parenteral ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              nutrition.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <u>Clinical Reference</u><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1. Chalmers RA, Roe CR, Stacey TE, et al: Urinary excretion of l- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              carnitine and acylcarnitines by patients with disorders of organic acid ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              metabolism: evidence for secondary insufficiency of l-carnitine. Ped ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Res 1984;18:1325-1328<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              2. Scaglia F, Wang YH, Singh RH, et al: Defective urinary carnitine ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              transport in heterozygotes for primary carnitine deficiency. Genet Med ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1998;1:34-39<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 78.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              3. Scaglia F, Longo N: Primary and secondary alterations of neonatal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 69.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              carnitine metabolism. Semin Perinatol 1999;23:152-161<br /> ) Tj
