1 0 0 1 102.0 638.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Free and total carnitine are measured by tandem mass spectrometry ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(MS/MS\) stable isotope dilution analysis. Hydrolysis enables ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 614.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              measurement of total carnitine, and esterified carnitine ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(acylcarnitine\) is calculated as the difference between the total and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 590.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              free carnitine. Quantification is enabled using deuterium-labeled ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              carnitine \(d[3]-carnitine\) added as internal standard. A selected ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 566.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              reaction monitoring \(SRM\) experiment is performed by MS/MS. The first ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 554.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mass spectrometer \(Q1\) detects carnitine and d[3]-carnitine precursors, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 542.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and transmits them to a collision cell \(Q2\) within the mass ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              spectrometer where they are fragmented. Specific fragments derived from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 518.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the carnitine and internal standard are monitored in the second mass ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 506.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              spectrometer \(Q3\). \(Stevens RD, Hillman SL, Worthy S, et al: Assay for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 494.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              free and total carnitine in human plasma using tandem mass ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              spectrometry. Clin Chem 2000;46:727-729\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 470.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  3 working days upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
