0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a General Lab or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 734.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Secreting neuroendocrine tumors are typically associated with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              catecholamine concentrations several times higher than the upper ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 710.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              reference intervals. Large elevations can be seen in life-threatening ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              illnesses and drug interferences. Common reasons for slight and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 686.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              moderate elevations include intense physical activity, emotional and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              physical stress, drug interferences, and improper specimen ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              collection.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 638.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Medications which may physiologically interfere with catecholamines and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              metabolites include amphetamines and amphetamine-like compounds, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 614.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              appetite suppressants, bromocriptine, buspirone, caffeine, carbidopa- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              levodopa \(Sinemet&#174;\), clonidine, dexamethasone, diuretics \(in doses ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 590.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              sufficient to deplete sodium\), ethanol, isoproterenol, methyldopa ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(Aldomet&#174;\), MAO inhibitors, nicotine, nose drops, propafenone ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 566.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(Rythmol\), reserpine, theophylline, tricyclic antidepressants, and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 554.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              vasodilators. The effects of some drugs on catecholamine results may ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 542.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              not be predictable.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 518.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              VMA, Catecholamines and Metanephrines may be done on same collection. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 506.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Alpha methylodopa \(Aldomet\) and Labetalol \(Normodyne\) will falsely ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 494.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              elevate the apparent concentration of urine catecholamines. Collection ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              containers available from pharmacy.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 470.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 458.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <strong class="style_red">Includes: Epidenphrine, Norepinephrine and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 446.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Dopamine.</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 422.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              If screening for Neuroblastoma, the following tests are suggested: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 410.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              CAT24 \(Catecholamines, Fractionated; Dopamine is included\), HVA24 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 398.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(Homovanillic Acid\), MET24 \(Metanephrines\), VMA24 \(Vanillylmandelic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Acid\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 362.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
