0.0000 Tw
(                              The Hematology Laboratory will make and review a smear if any of the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              following conditions apply:  \(1\) patient's first CBC sample AND results ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              meet laboratory review criteria; \(2\) questionable \(not necessarily ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              abnormal\) CBC results; \(3\) CBC results are significantly different from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              that of a previous specimen; \(4\) a physician specifically requests a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              smear review by Technologist or a "Pathologist Review Blood Smear". ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              EDTA samples are saved in the laboratory until 4:00 p.m. the day after ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              receipt.  Upon request, a smear could be made up until that time if ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              necessary.  However, as the specimen ages, cell disintegration and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 78.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              distortion may occur.  Stained smears are held in the laboratories for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 69.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              approximately two months.</pre> ) Tj
