(                    Comments  A CBC must be ordered to perform a differential.  Hematology ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              instruments are automated differential screening instruments that ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              identify WBC's by their size and staining activity.  It performs a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              complete cell identification that includes neutrophils, lymphocytes, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              monocytes, basophils, eosinophils and immature granulocytes. The ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              automated instruments count 32,000 white blood cells and statistically ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              provide a more accurate differential count than a manual differential. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              All differentials will be analyzed on the instrument first.  If the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              results fail the screening criteria, a manual differential will be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              performed.  Pathologist approval is required to perform a manual ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              differential on a specimen with an automated differential that passed ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 78.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the screening criteria. ) Tj
