(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Congenital disorders of glycosylation \(CDG\), formerly known as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              carbohydrate-deficient glycoprotein syndrome, are a group of more than ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              45 inherited metabolic disorders affecting several steps of the pathway ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              involved in the glycosylation of proteins. CDG are classified into 2 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              groups. Type I CDG is characterized by defects in the assembly or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              transfer of the dolichol-linked glycan, while type II involves ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              processing defects of the glycan. Apolipoprotein CIII \(Apo-CIII\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              isoforms, a protein with a single core 1 mucin type O-glycosylate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              protein, is a complementary evaluation for the CDG type II profile. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              This analysis will evaluate mucin type O-glycosylation, a defect that ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              happens in the Golgi apparatus, and will change the ratios, increasing ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the asialo or monoisalo forms and decreasing the fully sialilate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(disialo\) forms. In young children \(>1 month\) and in liver disease, the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Apo-CIII2 may be increased. Children younger than 6 months, and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              clinically suspected of having ATP6V0A2-CDG, may have normal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              transferrin profile with abnormal Apo-CIII profile.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <strong><u>Useful For</u></strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Screening for congenital disorders of glycosylation. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                        See:  <br />Carbohydrate Deficient Transferrin, Serum  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Affinity Chromatography/Mass Spectrometry \(MS\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  5 days upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
