0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  Unaffected samples will lack disease-associated <em>CEBPA</em> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mutations, but may harbor previously identified single nucleotide ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              polymorphisms \(SNPs\) that are reported as incidental findings.   ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Molecular Pathology/Diagnostics or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  In the bone marrow, the CCAAT/enhancer-binding protein, alpha \(CEBPA\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              is a myelomonocytic lineage-specific transcription factor that promotes ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              myeloid differentiation \(1\).  Mutations in the <em>CEBPA</em> gene have ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              been reported in acute myelogenous leukemia \(AML; 5-14% of cases\) and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              myelodysplastic syndromes \(2-7\).  In the absence of other genetic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              lesions known to confer a poor prognosis \(e.g., <em>FLT3</em>-ITD ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mutation\), mutations in <em>CEBPA</em> are associated with a favorable ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              prognosis for AML.  However, the benefit appears to be restricted to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cases in which there are biallelic <em>CEBPA</em> mutations, often ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              consisting of two discrete \(compound heterozygous\) mutations affecting ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              different functional domains of the CEBPA protein \(3-5\).  A variety of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              inactivating point mutations, deletions and insertions have been ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              described, requiring evaluation of the entire CEBPA coding ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              sequence.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <u>References</u><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1. Zhang P, et al. <em>Immunity</em> 2004;21\(6\):853-63.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              2. Nerlov C. <em>Nature Reviews Cancer</em> 2004;4\(5\):394-400.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              3. Dufour A, et al. <em>J Clin Oncol</em> 2010;28\(4\):570-7.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              4. Wouters BJ, et al. <em>Blood</em> 2009;113\(13\):3088-91.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              5. Taskesan E, et al. <em>Blood</em> 2011;117:2469-75.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              6. Gombart AF, et al. <em>Blood</em> 2002;99\(4\):1332-1340. <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              7. Shih LY, et al. <em>Clin Cancer Res</em> 2005;11\(5\):1821-26. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
