0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <strong>This mailout test requires pathologist approval for orders ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              during inpatient encounters.  Mailouts staff will not process order ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              without approval.  The pathologist covering mailouts approval can be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              reached at pager #5379.  If approval is given, the name of the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              pathologist can be selected in the drop-down menu to the right of the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              approval warning in Epic when ordering the test.</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Clinical features:  CHARGE syndrome refers to a specific set of birth ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              defects, including coloboma of the eye, heart defects, choanal atresia, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mental and growth retardation and ear anomalies or hearing loss. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Congenital anomalies, which when seen together are quite specific to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              CHARGE syndrome, include coloboma of the iris, retina, choroid and/or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              optic disc with or without microphthalmos; choanal atresia or stenosis; ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and hypoplastic semi-circular canals.  Cranial nerve dysfunction is a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              minor sign and include anosmia, neurosensory deafness, facial palsy ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and swallowing difficulties.  Ear abnormalities involving the helices, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              middle ear and inner ear are very common and were seen in 90% of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              affected individuals in one study \(Stromland, 2005\).  Affected ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              patients may also have genital abnormalities \(hypogonadotropic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hypogonadism\), pre- and post-natal growth deficiency, hypotonia, and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              characteristic hands \(broad palms with "hockey-stick" palmar crease, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              short fingers and small/unusual thumbs\).  The characteristic facial ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              appearance includes square face with broad prominent forehead, arched ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              eyebrows, large eyes with or without ptosis, prominent nasal bridge and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              columella, flat midface, small mouth and facial asymmetry.  CHARGE ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              syndrome encompasses additional nonspecific features such as mental ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              retardation, skeletal abnormalities, hypodontia, orofacial clefting, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              tracheoesophageal fistula, and urinary tract and renal anomalies.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Reasons for referral:<pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1. Confirmation of the clinical diagnosis ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              2. Differential diagnosis from the 22q11 deletion spectrum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 \(VCFS/DiGeorge syndrome\), VACTERAL association, PAX2 mutations and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 Retinoic embryopathy ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              3. Development of appropriate evaluation and management plan ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              4. Genetic counseling ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              5. Prenatal diagnosis in at-risk pregnancies</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Please print, complete and submit the following forms to the lab, with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the specimen and the A-1a Miscellaneous Request:  <a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              href="http://www.genedx.com/wp- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              content/uploads/crm_docs/icd_chd.pdf">Informed Consent for DNA ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Testing</a> and the <a href="http://www.genedx.com/wp-content/uploads/crm_docs/Rare_Disorders_Req.pdf">Sample ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Submission Form - Testing Services for Rare Mendelian Disorders</a> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              from GeneDx DNA Diagnostic Experts. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  See report  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  9-10 weeks upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
