(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 731.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Computer code for sterile specimens = C ANA1 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Computer code for non-sterile specimens = C ANA2 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 702.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Tissue or aspirates are preferred rather than swabs.  Fluid collections ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 693.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              should be aspirated through disinfected tissue or skin.  For ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              superficial ulcers, collect material from below the surface \(after ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              surface debridement or use a needle and syringe\).  Submit specimens ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 664.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              using anaerobic transport media: BBL Port-A-Cul anaerobic collection ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              jar \(MH09109\) for tissue or ACT II tube system for fluid and swab ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              specimens \(MH07787\). A sterile screw-cap container \(MH04506\) may be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              used for tissue if transported to the microbiology lab immediately \(add ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              drops of sterile saline to keep small pieces of tissue moist\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Anaerobic flora is prevalent on mucosal surfaces of the oral cavity, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              upper respiratory, gastrointestinal, and genital tracts; specimens ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              collected from these sites should not ordinarily be cultured for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              anaerobic bacteria. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The following is a list of specimens that are likely to be contaminated ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with anaerobic normal flora and are NOT routinely accepted for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              anaerobic culture. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Throat or nasopharyngeal swabs ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Gingival or other intraoral surface swabs ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Expectorated sputum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Sputum obtained by nasotracheal or endotracheal suction ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Bronchial washings ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Voided or catheterized urine ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Vaginal or cervical swabs ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Gastric and small bowel contents \(except for "blind loop" or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 bacterial overgrowth syndrome\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Feces \(except for specific etiologic agents such as C. difficile ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 and C. botulinum\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                -Rectal swabs ) Tj
