0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  <pre>Antibody concentration of > 0.1 IU/mL is usually considered ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              protective. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Responder status is determined according to the ratio of a one-month, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              post-vaccination sample to pre-vaccination concentration of Diphtheria ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              IgG Abs as follows: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1.  If the post-vaccination concentration is less than 1.0 IU/mL, the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              patient is considered a nonresponder. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              2.  If the post-vaccination concentration is greater than or equal to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1.0 IU/mL, a patient with a ratio of less than 1.5 is a nonresponder, a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ratio of 1.5 to less than 3.0, is a weak responder, and a ratio of 3.0 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              or greater, is a good responder. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              3.  IF the pre-vaccination concentraiton is greaer than 1.0 IU/mL, it ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              may be difficult to assess the response based on a ratio alone.  A ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              post-vaccination concentration above 2.5 IU in this case is usually ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              adequate.</pre>  ) Tj
