1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  This assay is a rapid in vitro microwell EIA for the detection of Shiga ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 640.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              toxins I and II \(verotoxins\) in stool specimens.  The test is intended ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 630.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              for use as an aid in the diagnosis of enterohemorrhagic Escherichia ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 621.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              coli \(EHEC\) infection. Shiga toxin testing of stool specimens provides ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 611.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              better sensitivity than standard culture methods for the E. coli ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              O157:H7 serotype and non-O157 serotypes. Testing of broth cultures, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 592.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              rather than the stool specimens themselves, is performed because the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 582.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              amount of free fecal Shiga toxin in stools is often low.  All Shiga ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 573.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              toxin positive broths \(or presumptive E. coli O157:H7 isolates\) will be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 563.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              forwarded to the University Hygienic Laboratory for confirmatory ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 554.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              testing and genetic characterization.  Shiga toxin testing is included ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 544.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in routine stool cultures as recommended by <a href= http://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5538a3.htm>Centers for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 534.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Disease Control</a> \(CDC\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 515.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
