(                    Comments  The anion gap or electrolyte balance is calculated by the formula Na -  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 750.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(Cl +HCO3\).  In normal individuals most of the anion gap is due to  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 741.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              protein. When an unmeasured anion such as ketones, lactate, formate, or  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 731.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              oxalate is present an elevated anion gap results. While the values for  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the anion gap are method dependent, there is agreement that an anion  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 712.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              gap > 16 is considered elevated. The reasons for a decreased anion gap  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 702.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              are fewer and include low proteins, multiple myeloma \(tend to be  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 693.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              positively charged\) and bromide ingestion \(falsely counted as  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              chloride\). Patients may have a normal anion gap and still have  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              acidosis. This is known as hyperchloremic acidosis where an elevated  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 664.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              chloride compensates for the decreased bicarbonate. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
