1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Normal serum concentrations of erythropoietin for 95% of individuals ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with normal hematocrits range from 4-27 mU/mL. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              As the hematocrit is lowered by iron deficiency, aplastic or hemolytic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              anemia, the concentration of erythropoietin increases as shown in the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              graph below. In the absence of anemia, elevated concentrations are seen ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in renal tumors, as a manifestation of renal transplant rejection, and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in secondary polycythemia. Low values may be observed in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hemochromatosis. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Decreased erythropoietin concentrations with an elevated hematocrit are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              observed in patients with polycythemia rubra vera, and with a decreased ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hematocrit in patients with HIV infection who are receiving AZT. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Patients on AZT who have anemia and erythropoietin concentrations of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              less than or equal to 500 mU/mL, may benefit from therapy with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              recombinant EPO \(NEJM 322:1488-1493, 1990\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
