0.0000 Tw
(                              <td width="110" valign="top" align="center">Pink top tube</td> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </table> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  1.5 mL Plasma to reference laboratory.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(         Rejection Criteria:  Grossly hemolyzed.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  Results may be significantly elevated \(ie, >900 RU/mL\) in normal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              infants <3 months of age.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              3 months-17 years: < or =230 RU/mL<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              > or =18 years: < or =180 RU/mL  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Fibroblast growth factor 23 \(FGF23\) is a major regulator of phosphate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              homeostasis. It may act in concert with several other less well ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              characterized phosphate regulators.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              FGF23 is secreted primarily by bone, followed by thymus, heart, brain ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and, in low levels, by several other tissues. It is coexpressed with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the X-linked phosphate-regulating endopeptides \(PHEX\). High serum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              phosphate levels stimulate FGF23 expression and secretion through as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              yet poorly understood mechanisms. PHEX appears to modulate this ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              process, possibly in part through cleavage of FGF23. Only intact FGF23 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              is considered bioactive. It interacts with a specific receptor on renal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              tubular cells, decreasing expression of type IIa sodium/phosphate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cotransporters, resulting in decreased phosphate reabsorption. In ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              addition, gene transcription of 1-a-hydroxylase is downregulated, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              reducing bioactive 1,25-dihydroxy vitamin D \(1,25-2OH-VitD\), thereby ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              further decreasing phosphate reabsorption. Eventually, falling serum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              phosphate levels lead to diminished FGF23 secretion, closing the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              feedback loop.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Measurement of serum FGF23 can assist in diagnosis and management of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              disorders of phosphate and bone metabolism in patients with either ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              normal or impaired renal function. When FGF23 levels are pathologically ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              elevated in individuals with normal renal function, hypophosphatemia, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with or without osteomalacia, ensues. This can occur with rare, usually ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              benign, mixed connective tissue tumors that contain characteristic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              complex vascular structures, osteoclast-like giant cells, cartilaginous ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              elements and dystrophic calcifications. These neoplasms secrete FGF23 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ectopically and autonomously \(oncogenic osteomalacia\). In less than 1/4 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of cases, a different benign or malignant, soft tissue tumor type, or, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              extremely rarely, a carcinoma, may be the cause of paraneoplastic FGF23 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              secretion. In either scenario, complete removal of the tumor cures the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              oncogenic osteomalacia.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Hypophosphatemia and skeletal abnormalities are also observed in X- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              linked hypophosphatemia \(XLH\) and autosomal dominant hypophosphatemic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              rickets \(ADHR\). In XLH, mutations of PHEX reduce its negative ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              modulatory effect on bioactive FGF23 secretion. In ADHR, FGF23 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mutations render it resistant to proteolytic cleavage, thereby ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              increasing FGF23 levels. However, not all FGF23 mutations increase ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              renal phosphate secretions. Mutations that impair FGF23 signaling, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              rather than increase its protease resistance, are associated with the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              syndrome of familial tumoral calcinosis \(ectopic calcifications\) with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hyperphosphatemia.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              In patients with renal failure, FGF23 contributes to renal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              osteodystrophy. The patient's kidneys can no longer excrete sufficient ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              amounts of phosphate. This leads to marked increases in FGF23 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              secretions in a futile compensatory response, aggravating the 1,25-2OH- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              VitD deficiency of renal failure and the consequent secondary ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hyperparathyroidism.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 78.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <strong><u>Useful for</u>:</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 69.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              *Diagnosing and monitoring oncogenic osteomalacia<br /> ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(284) Tj
1 0 0 1 355.18 37 Tm
(Updated:Mon Aug 26 14:13:27 2013) Tj
