0.0000 Tw
(                              Preferred minimum: 5 mL heparinized whole blood from fasting patient ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Absolute minimum: 2 mL heparinized whole blood from fasting ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              patient</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(         Rejection Criteria:  Sample must be received at reference laboratory within 48 hours of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              collection, collect Monday through Thursday only; do not collect on ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Fridays, holidays, day before a holiday, or weekends. Specimen cannot ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              be frozen.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <2 years:                         20.1-79.8 mU/g Hemoglobin ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Greater than or equal to 2 years: 12.1-39.7 mU/g Hemoglobin</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Whole blood to be washed at reference laboratory.  If specimen cannot ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              arrive within 48 hours, please send washed erythrocytes.  Draw blood in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              a green top \(heparin\) tubes\(s\) from a fasting patient \(4 hour ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              preferred, nonfasting acceptable\), and send 5.0 mL of heparinized whole ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              blood refrigerated. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Clinical information: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Three clinically important inborn errors of galactose metabolism that ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              result in galactosemia have been described.  The genetic disturbance is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              expressed as a deficiency of galactokinase, galactose-1-phosphate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              uridyltransferase, or UDP galactose-4-epimerase, the enzymes catalyzing ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the reactions in converting galactose to glucose.  The transferase ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              deficiency is the most common.  Galactokinase deficiency results in a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              milder variant of galactosemia than that which results from GALT ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              deficiency.  The epimerase deficiency is like the kinase deficiency and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              is much more rare than the transferase deficiency. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Useful for: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Diagnosis of the second most common cause of galactosemia \(ie, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              galactokinase deficiency\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Interpretation: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Values <20.1 mU/g of hemoglobin suggest galactokinase deficiency.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Radioisotopic  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  2 weeks upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
