1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Adult Preferred Minimum: 5.0 mL whole blood from 6 mL pink top ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                \(K2 EDTA\) tube. Collect specimen from a fasting patient. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Adult/Pediatric Absolute minimum: 2.0 mL whole blood from 6 mL pink ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 top \(K2 EDTA\) tube. Collect specimen from a fasting patient.</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(         Rejection Criteria:  Specimen cannot be frozen.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  Descriptive report  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              This assay is useful for determining the likely genotype when ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              quantitative galactose-1-phosphate uridyltransferase \(GALT\) data ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              suggests a GG or DG genotype \(a patient with a GG genotype must be on a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              galactose-free diet\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Useful for: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1\) Determining the exact biochemical phenotype when quantitative GALT ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(galactose-1-phosphate uridyltransferase \(GALT\) deficiency suggests a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              GG or DG phenotype ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              2\) A quantitative GALT level is used in addition to the isoelectric ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              focusing for accurate interpretation ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              3\) Determining biochemical phenotypes of siblings, when parental ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              specimens are co-run for both quantitative and isoelectric focusing ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              banding data ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              There are a variety of biochemical phenotypes in galactosemia and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              quantitative data is only suggestive of the phenotype for a particular ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              individual.  An interpretive report is provided. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              CAUTIONS: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The phenotype of a neonate can be arrived at with greater confidence ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              when the parents' phenotypes are also established. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Since transfusion results in replacement of significant number of red ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cells, the assay should be deferred for 90 days post-transfusion.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                        See:  <br />Galactosemia Confirmation with Reflex to Galt Gene Analysis,  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Whole Blood  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                See Appendix  See Additional Information: <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
