(                              Three types of enzymatic deficiencies, galactokinase, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              galactose-1-phosphate uridyltransferase \(GPUT\), and uridine diphosphate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(UDP\) galactose-4-epimerase are responsible for galactosemia, an ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              autosomal recessive inborn error of galactose metabolism. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Clinical Information: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The most common form of galactosemia \(classic galactosemia\) is caused ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              by homozygous inheritance of abnormal GPUT phenotypic designation \(GG\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and results in absence of GPUT activity and accumulation of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              galactose-1-phosphate \(G-1-P\) in erythrocytes.  Classic galactosemia is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              characterized by failure to thrive, vomiting, liver disease, cataracts, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and developmental delay. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Useful for: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Monitoring dietary therapy for classic galactosemia \(total GPUT ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              deficiency\), galactosemia-Duarte \(GD\) patients, or rarely, patients ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with UDP galactose-4-epimerase deficiency. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Interpretation: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The reference values provided are for nongalactosemics and for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              galactosemic patients on a galactose-restricted diet. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The goal of treatment of a galactosemic patient is to have G-1-P levels ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              as low as possible, but no higher than 125 mcg/g of hemoglobin. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Cautions: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Not a screening test for galactosemia</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Ultraviolet, Enzymatic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              This assay is a quantitative measure of the galactose-1-phosphate and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              is useful for monitoring the dietary management of galactosemics.  This ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              assay should not be used for the diagnosis of galactosemia.</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  2 weeks upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(            Testing Schedule  Testing performed on Tuesdays and Thursdays.  ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(Updated:Mon Aug 26 14:13:27 2013) Tj
1 0 0 1 506.32 37 Tm
(309) Tj
