(                              <tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 693.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <td width="110" valign="top" align="center">Pink top tube</td> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </tr> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </table> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  Preferred Minimum:  2 mL plasma<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Absolute Minimum:  0.5 mL plasma  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  < or =6 hours: 100-650 pg/mL<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1-2 days: 70-450 pg/mL<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              2-4 days: 100-650 pg/mL<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              4-14 days: declining gradually to adult levels<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              >14 days: < or =80 pg/mL \(range based on 95% confidence limits\) <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Glucagon levels are inversely related to blood glucose levels at all ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ages. This is particularly pronounced at birth and shortly thereafter, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              until regular feeding patterns are established. This explains the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              higher levels immediately after birth, which then first fall as the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              glucagon release mobilizes the infants glucose stores, then rise again ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              as stores are depleted, finally normalizing towards adult levels as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              regular feeding patterns are established.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Useful for diagnosis and follow-up of glucagonomas and other glucagon- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              producing tumors. <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Assessing diabetic patients with problematic hyper- or hypoglycemic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              episodes \(extremely limited utility\). <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Glucagon is routinely measured along with serum glucose, insulin, and  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              C- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              peptide levels, during the mixed-meal test employed in the diagnostic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              workup of suspected postprandial hypoglycemia. However, it plays only a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              minor role in the interpretation of this test.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <strong><u>Cautions</u>:</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Results obtained with different glucagon assays can differ ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              substantially. This can be caused by use of different calibration ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              standards. Different glucagon assays may also exhibit variable cross- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              reactivity with different isoforms of glucagon, not all of which are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              biologically active. Some assays, including this one, remove ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              biologically inactive isoforms before measurement, while others do not. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              All these factors contribute to the differences between different ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              assays. Serial measurements should, therefore, always be performed ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              using the same assay. <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Precise reference ranges for appropriate glucagon responses for given ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              blood glucose ranges are not well established and vary widely from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              assay to assay. Expert advice should be sought when interpreting ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              inappropriately low glucagon levels or when interpreting glucagon, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              insulin, and C-peptide levels obtained during mixed-meal testing. <br  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Tumor marker tests, including glucagon, are not specific for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              malignancy. All immunometric assays can, on rare occasions, be subject ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              to hooking at extremely high analyte concentrations \(false-low ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              results\), heterophilic antibody interference \(false-high results\), or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              autoantibody interference \(unpredictable effects\). If the laboratory ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              result does not fit the clinical picture, these possibilities should be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              considered. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                See Appendix  See Additional Information: <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Fasting Specimen Requirements<br />Specimens Requiring Immediate  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Delivery  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Immunoassay Following Extraction  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  4 working days upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
