0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <strong class="style_red">This test requires approval of Clinical ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pathology Resident on-call \(pager #3404\).</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Note that the "Ethylene Glycol, Plasma" provides more rapid ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              determination of ethylene glycol plasma concentrations. The "Ethylene ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Glycol, Plasma" test is reflexively ordered if the unexplained osmolar ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              gap is greater than 15 and may also be directly ordered in cases of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              suspected ethylene glycol ingestion <strong class="style_red">or for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              monitoring ethylene glycol plasma concentrations in patients receiving ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              treatment for ethylene glycol ingestion</strong>. This procedure ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              individually quantitates ethylene glycol.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The glycols by gas chromatography tests may be ordered if there is an ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              interference with the "Ethylene Glycol, Plasma" test or if quantitation ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of propylene glycol is needed. This procedure individually quantitates ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ethylene glycol and propylene glycol. Ethylene glycol is commonly found ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in many automobile antifreezes. Propylene glycol is found in some ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              intravenous drug formulations as a solvent/diluent \(e.g., diazepam, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              lorazepam, etomidate, and phenytoin\) and is also found in a small ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              number of automobile antifreezes \(e.g., Sierra\).<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              References:<br /> ) Tj
