(           Collection Medium  Miscellaneous container; contact laboratory  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(         Rejection Criteria:  Bags not fully inflated or only one of the two bags submitted; breath ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 712.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              collected in tubes; refrigerated or frozen specimens; collect Monday ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 702.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              through Thursday only; do not collect on Fridays, holidays, day before ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 693.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              a holiday, or weekends.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 683.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <strong class="style_red">Pediatric specimens from persons 17 years or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 664.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              younger.</strong>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  Negative  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Testing kits are available from Specimen Control, 6240 RCP. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Patient preparation: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The patient should fast and abstain from smoking for 1 hour prior to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              test administration  The patient should not have taken antibiotics, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              proton pump inhibitors or bismuth preparations within the previous 14 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              days.  These include: Prilosec, Prevacid, Aciphex, Nexium, and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pepto-Bismol.  When used to monitor treatment, the test should be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              performed four weeks after cessation of definitive therapy. The patient ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              should be informed that the Pranactin-Citric drink that will be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              administered contains phenylalanine.  Phenylketonurics restrict dietary ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              phenylalanine. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Test administration: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                1\) Label breath collection bags with patient name, MRN, date and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   time of collection, and designate Pre \(blue\) or Post \(pink\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                2\) Collect the  baseline breath sample: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   a\) Remove cap from collection bag \(blue\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   b\) Have patient take a deep breath, pause momentarily then exhale ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                      into the mouthpiece of the bag filling it completely. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   c\) Replace cap on the bag. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                3\) Prepare Pranactin-Citric solution: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   a\) Empty packet from test kit into the cup provided. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   b\) Add drinking water up to the fill line \(raised ridge\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   c\) Replace lid; swirl for up to two minutes until completely ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                      dissolved. Solution should be clear. The solution is stable up ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                      to 60 minutes at room temperature. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                4\) Instruct patient to drink the solution without stopping using the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   straw provided.  Advise the patient not to "rinse" the mouth with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   the solution before swallowing. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                5\) Set timer for 15 minutes. Start timer as soon as the patient has ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   completed drinking. Patient should sit quietly without eating, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   drinking, or smoking. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                6\) Prepare the post sample collection \(pink\) bag. At exactly 15 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   minutes, have the patient take a deep breath, pause momentarily ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                   and then exhale to fill the second sample collection bag \(pink\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Note: for a valid result, the post sample must be collected within 13 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              to 18 minutes after administration of the Pranactin-Citric Solution. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Return kit to Specimen Control, 6240 RCP. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Sample stability: 1 week only-must reach reference laboratory within a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              week of collection.  Critical ambient.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                See Appendix  See Additional Information: <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Fasting Specimen Requirements  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Infrared Spectrophotometric  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
