1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Please print, complete, and submit the <a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              href="http://www.miravistalabs.com/Files/pdf/Req_2011_Ver_4.pdf"> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              MiraVista Diagnostics Test Requisition</a> with the specimen and A-1a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <pre><strong>Guidelines for Use</strong> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              As an aid in rapid diagnosis of disseminated or acute pulmonary ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              histoplasmosis. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Testing both urine and serum offers the highest sensitivity, as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               some patients may have negative results in one but positive results in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               the other specimen type. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Serum, plasma and other specimens that appear to contain blood ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               are treated with EDTA/heat to allow dissociation of immune complexes. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               This pre-treatment can increase sensitivity by 95% in specimens that ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               previously tested negative. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Serum is particularly useful for monitoring therapy \(see below\), ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               and should be tested if initially positive. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;CSF or BALF improves sensitivity in meningitis or pulmonary ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               histoplasmosis. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              False-positive and false-negative results occur. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Antigen results must be correlated with clinical and other ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               laboratory findings. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Repeat the antigen testing if the result is inconsistent with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               other findings or the sole basis for diagnosis. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Culture and serology are recommended if antigen is the sole  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              basis ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               for diagnosis. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Weak-positive results, <0.6 to 3.9 ng/mL, are less likely to be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               reproducible and should be verified by repeat testing. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;A positive result in serum with a negative result in urine is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               rare and is cause for concern about a false-positive result caused by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               anti-rabbit or heterophile antibodies. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Cross-reactions occur in blastomycosis, coccidioidomycosis, African ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              histoplasmosis, paracoccidioidomycosis and penicilliosis. Correct ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              diagnosis can usually be distinguished by epidemiologic, clinical or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              other laboratory findings. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Monitoring therapy: Antigen declines with effective therapy. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Failure of antigen to decline by at least 20% during the first ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               month of therapy and 20% during subsequent 3-month intervals suggests ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               treatment failure. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Suggest testing after one month of therapy and then every 3-4 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               months until negative. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Antigen declines more rapidly in serum than urine, and antigen ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               concentration in serum is less likely to be affected by hydration ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               status than is the concentration in urine. If the baseline serum is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               positive, it should be monitored until negative, and then urine should ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               be monitored until negative. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 69.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Diagnosing relapse: Antigen increases at the time of relapse in up to ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(Updated:Mon Aug 26 14:13:27 2013) Tj
1 0 0 1 506.32 37 Tm
(371) Tj
