(                               reproducible and should be verified by repeat testing. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;A positive result in serum with a negative result in urine is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               rare and is cause for concern about a false-positive result caused by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               anti-rabbit or heterophile antibodies. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Cross-reactions occur in blastomycosis, coccidioidomycosis, African ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              histoplasmosis, paracoccidioidomycosis and penicilliosis. Correct ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              diagnosis can usually be distinguished by epidemiologic, clinical or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              other laboratory findings. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Monitoring therapy: Antigen declines with effective therapy. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Failure of antigen to decline by at least 20% during the first ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               month of therapy and 20% during subsequent 3-month intervals suggests ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               treatment failure. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Suggest testing after one month of therapy and then every 3-4 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               months until negative. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Antigen declines more rapidly in serum than urine, and antigen ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               concentration in serum is less likely to be affected by hydration ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               status than is the concentration in urine. If the baseline serum is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               positive, it should be monitored until negative, and then urine should ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               be monitored until negative. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Diagnosing relapse: Antigen increases at the time of relapse in up to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              90% of cases. The magnitude of change suggestive of relapse varies over ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the wide range of antigen concentrations. A 3 unit increase is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              concerning for relapse in specimens with results < 20 ng/mL compared to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              a 15% increase in specimens with results > 20 ng/mL. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Suggest testing every 3 months during therapy and at the time of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               suspected relapse. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              &#8226;Most sensitive if both serum and urine are tested at the time of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                               suspected relapse.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
