72 792 m
523 792 l
S
BT
0 G
1 i 0 J 0 j 0.1 w 10 M []0 d
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 797 Tm
() Tj
1 0 0 1 367.98 797 Tm
(Pathology Laboratory Handbook) Tj
/F10 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 758.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              B ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              BP_exp_Feb_13.pdf">G-2d16 Consent for Human Immunodeficiency Virus ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 734.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(HIV\)-Related Testing Due to a Healthcare Worker Exposure to Body ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Fluids to be used for Minors \(<18 Years of Age\)</a></pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              This test replaces "HIV 1/2 Combined Antibodies" \(ELISA reflexed to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 686.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Western\), "HIV Antigen", and "HIV, Rapid" \(OraQuick\).   ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                See Appendix  See Additional Information: <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Bloodborne Pathogens  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Chemiluminescent microparticle immunoassay \(CMIA\) run on the Abbott ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 638.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Architect platform.  This assay uses antibodies against both anti-HIV ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              antibodies and a conserved epitope on the p24 antigen.  A patient that ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 614.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              has anti-HIV antibodies and/or HIV antigen in plasma can test ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 602.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              positive.  This test thereby can detect both acute and chronic HIV ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 590.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              infection.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
