1 0 0 1 102.0 323.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              </table> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 304.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  Preferred Minimum:  collect TWO full 5 mL red top tubes to yield 5 mL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 294.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              serum.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 285.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 275.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Absolute Minimum: 3-5 mL serum from TWO full red top tubes.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 266.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  By report  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 256.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 246.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 237.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Flow Cytometry ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 227.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              This method uses a panel of purified HLA Class I antigens derived from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 218.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              30-50 different unrelated individuals that are pooled or coupled to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 208.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              microbeads.  The patient's serum is mixed with microbeads, then washed, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 198.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and stained with an anti-human IgG Fluorescent conjugate.  The ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 189.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              microbeads are then analyzed for immunofluorescence by flow cytometry ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 179.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              to detect HLA Class I IgG antibodies.  The results are reported as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 170.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              panel reactive \(PRA\) present or absent. A PRA with positive ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 160.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              fluorescence of the HLA-bead population that is greater than the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 150.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              negative control serum and the patient's autologous serum tested ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 141.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              against beads conjugated with human serum albumin will be reported as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 131.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              positive. It has been demonstrated that this flow cytometric ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 122.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              methodology can detect antibodies at a more sensitive level than ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 112.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              conventional lymphocyte cytotoxicity procedures.  In addition, flow ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 102.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cytometry only detects antibodies of the IgG isotype and not IgM ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 93.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              antibodies, which are usually indicative of autoantibodies.</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 83.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  5 working days upon receipt in reference laboratory  ) Tj
