(                              95% of the circulatig IGF-I and IGF-II. <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 734.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              IGFBP-3 is growth hormone \(GH\) responsive. Thus, levels are high in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cromegaly and low in hypopituitarism, and levels increase in GH- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 710.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              deficient children after GH administration. <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 686.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Other causes of short stature that result in reduced IGFBP-3 levels ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 674.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              include poorly controlled diabetes. The IGFBP-3 assay is useful in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              assessing nutritional status, since IGFBP-3 decreases during both ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
