0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Methodology of blood lead testing changed on 4/20/2011 from atomic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              absorption \(AA\) to the LeadCare II instrument.  This allows for 24/7 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              availability of lead concentrations compared to the previous schedule ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of routine testing performed only one day/week.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              By state of Iowa requirements, all lead concentrations of 15 &#956;g/dL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              or greater by the LeadCare II instrument must be confirmed with a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              venous sample analyzed by a reference method such as atomic absorption ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              or inductively-coupled plasma mass spectrometry \(ICP-MS\).  This ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              requirement is fulfilled by having the test "LEAD, VENOUS CONFIRMATION ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              BY ICP-MS" \(Epic LAB7479\) available.  For the confirmatory test, only a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              venous specimen is acceptable \(i.e., no capillary sample ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              allowable\).<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              If the lead concentration is 15 &#956;g/dL or greater by LeadCare II ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              test and sufficient venous specimen is available for confirmatory ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              testing, the Clinical Chemistry laboratory will reflexively send out ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the confirmatory testing and the following comment will be appended to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the LeadCare II result:<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              "This venous specimen has a blood lead concentration of 15 &#956;g/dL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              by the LeadCare II instrument and has been sent-out for confirmation by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              a reference method.  This is in accord with state of Iowa ) Tj
