1 0 0 1 102.0 758.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              quantification can be done by densitometric measurement of Lp\(a\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cholesterol. This method measures only the cholesterol contained in the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 734.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Lp\(a\) particles and is thus not influenced by the relative size of the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              apo\(a\) size, it may provide a more specific assessment of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 710.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cardiovascular risk than Lp\(a\) mass measurement. Lp\(a\) cholesterol ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              measurement may be used in concert with Lp\(a\) mass determination, or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 686.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              may be used as a stand-alone test for assessment of risk. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
