1 0 0 1 102.0 654.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  See report  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre>This mailout test requires pathologist approval for orders during ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              inpatient encounters.  Mailouts staff will not process order without ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              approval.  The pathologist covering mailouts approval can be reached at ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              pager #5379.  If approval is given, the name of the pathologist can be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              selected in the drop-down menu to the right of the approval warning in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Epic when ordering the test. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Genetic analysis is very important for identifying all mutation ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              carriers within the LQTS family.  Once identified, silent carriers of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              LQTS genetic defects may be treated with beta-blockers for prophylaxis ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of life-threatening arrhythmias.  Furthermore, silent mutation carriers ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              should receive genetic counseling to learn about the risk of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              transmitting LQTS to offspring. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              In patients affects by LQTS, genetic analysis is useful for risk ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              stratification and for making therapeutic decisions. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Risk Stratification ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 *Genetic testing is often useful in probands with a clinical ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                  diagnosis of LQTS to provide more accurate risk stratification ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                  and to guide therapeutic strategies. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                 *It has been shown that the interplay between genetic defect, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                  QT duration, and gender may provide an algorithm for risk ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                  stratification. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Genetic testing that can detect a mutation which may cause cardiac ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              channelopathies, rare, potentially lethal heart conditions.  The tests ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              can reduce uncertainty and find the specific causes of cardiac ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              channelopathies, the test can: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                *Help diagnose a patient's disease ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                *Guide treatment options ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                *Determine whether family members are at risk ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Patients presenting with: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Unexplained syncope ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Onset of symptoms typically occurs during childhood and adolescence ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Family Hx of sudden cardiac death ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Unexplained VT/VF or TdP ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Prolonged QT interval ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              KCNQ1 \(LQT1\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              KCNH2 \(LQT1\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              SCN5A \(LQT3\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              KCNE1 \(LQTS\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              KCNE2 \(LQT6\)</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  4-6 weeks  ) Tj
