1 0 0 1 102.0 486.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              as "POSITIVE".  Prior to September 14, 2010, the laboratory had the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 477.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              routine practice of doing PEG precipitation for all prolactin ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 467.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              concentrations greater than the gender-specific reference range.  An ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 458.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              analysis of results from January 2006-July 2010 revealed that the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 448.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              incidence of macroprolactin in quantities sufficient to cause PEG ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 438.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              precipitation results to be less than 50% of the total prolactin ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 429.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              concentration is very low \(<0.1%\). Consequently, the macroprolactin ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 419.6 Tm
