(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <u>The reference laboratory offers a known familial variant test. If ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              you want to order the known familial variant version of the test, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              please order LAB7858</u>. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Analysis is performed by bi-directional sequencing of the coding ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              regions and splice sites of exons 2-10 of the MEN1 gene.  Mutations ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              found in the first person of a family to be tested are confirmed by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              repeat analysis using sequencing, restriction fragment analysis, or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              other appropriate method. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Germline MEN1 gene mutations have been found in 75-90% of patients with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              a clinical diagnosis of MEN1, regardless of family history.  This ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              sequencing approach is expected to identify >95% of existing small ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              intragenic mutations.</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
