1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Stool culture only assesses for the presence of \(listed roughly in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              order of prevalence in Iowa\) Campylobacter, Salmonella, E. coli O157 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and other shiga-toxin producing E. coli, Shigella, and a few other rare ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              enteric pathogens.  These are food- or water-borne bacteria that are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              very unlikely to be acquired in the hospital. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Stool cultures are therefore not performed for patients who have been ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hospitalized greater than 3 days without laboratory consultation \(page ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the microbiology resident on call at 4903 for consultation\).  Specimens ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              from inpatients who are in-house greater than 3 days without ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              preapproval will be rejected. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              See "Surveillance Culture" for Bone Marrow Transplant and other ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              immunocompromised patients to detect overgrowth of normal flora by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Staph aureus, yeast, or a gram negative bacillus.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                        See:  <br />Bacterial Culture  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
