1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Mycophenolate mofetil \(CellCept\) is a new immunosuppressive agent ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              useful in organ transplantation. It is approved for use in renal, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hepatic, and cardiac transplants. When mycophenolate mofetil enters the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              blood, it is immediately metabolized to the active drug, mycophenolic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              acid \(MPA\), which inhibits inosine monophosphate dehydrogenase and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              interferes with the de novo pathway of guanosine nucleotide synthesis ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              selectively in lymphocytes. MPA inhibits proliferative responses of T- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and B-lymphocytes to both mitogenic and allospecific stimulation. MPA ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              acts in the same fashion as azathioprine, and MPA is suggested as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              replacement therapy for azathioprine. The drug is deactivated by the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hepatic enzyme, uridine diphosphate glucuronosyltransferase \(UGT\) to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              form mycophenolic acid glucuronide \(MPA-G\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The principle clinical problem encountered in MPA therapy is excessive ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              immunosuppression, which predisposes the patient to systemic infection. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Measurement of the blood level of MPA and MPA-G can be useful to guide ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              therapy. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Monitoring is recommended immediately after transplant up to 3 weeks ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              after therapy is initiated to evaluate dosing adequacy.  Additional ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              monitoring is indicated if the MPA level is not in the therapeutic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              range or if a major change in health status occurs. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Correct interpretation requires a trough serum specimen \(just before ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the next regular dose\). Specimens drawn at other times in the dosing ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cycle are likely to have higher MPA levels. In these cases, the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              reference range does not apply.</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Tandem Mass Spectrometry \(MS/MS\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  4 days upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(Updated:Mon Aug 26 14:13:27 2013) Tj
1 0 0 1 506.32 37 Tm
(509) Tj
ET
