(                              Reference ranges in adults reflect 95th percentiles for NT-pro-BNP ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              levels in patients without congestive heart failure \(CHF\).  Knowledge ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of each individual patient's NT-proBNP range may be more useful than ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              using similar cut-points for every patient. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              For adult chronic CHF patients according to New York Heart Association ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(NYHA\) Functional Class for NT-proBNP levels in pg/mL: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                          Mean     5th percentile     95th percentile ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Class I:    1015            33               3410 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Class II:   1666           103               6567 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Class III:  3029           126               10449 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Class IV:   3465           148               12188 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pediatric reference ranges for patients 18 years and younger are from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              reference \(1\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Among patients with dyspnea, NT-proBNP is highly sensitive for the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              detection of acute CHF.  In addition, a NT-proBNP < 300 pg/mL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              effectively rules out acute CHF, with 99% negative predictive value. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Elevations in NT-proBNP levels may be observed in states other than ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              left ventricular congestive failure including: acute coronary ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              syndromes, right heart strain/failure \(including pulmonary embolism and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cor pulmonale\), critical illness, and renal failure.  Falsely low NT- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              proBNP in CHF patients may be observed in increased body mass index. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <u>References</u>: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(1\) Nir A et al.  Pediatr Cardiol 30:3-8, 2009.</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a General Lab or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The N-terminal Pro-Brain Natriuretic Peptide \(Pro-BNP\) is an assay used ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              as an aid in the diagnosis of individuals suspected of having ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              congestive heart failure.  The test is further indicated for the risk ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 98.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              stratification of patients with acute coronary syndrome and congestive ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              heart failure.  The test may also be used as an aid in the assessment ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 78.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of increased risk of cardiovascular events and mortality in patients at ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 69.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              risk for heart failure who have stable coronary artery disease. ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
