0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Adult - 5 mL; red top tube ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pediatric - 2 mL; red top tube</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  ANCA screen and titer: <1:40 Titer, includes interpretative report.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Immunopathology or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Please include relevant clinical information on test order form. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Test includes both C-ANCA and P-ANCA screening and titering.  MPO and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              PR3 confirmatory tests are performed if screen is positive or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              inconclusive.  Anti-neutrophil cytoplasmic antibodies are associated ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              primarily with two groups of diseases: systemic necrotizing ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              vasculitis/glomerulonephritis and inflammatory bowel and liver ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              disease. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Because the laboratory testing  strategies are different for these two ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              groups of disease, different tests must be ordered for each of these ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              workups.  "ANCA" is the test to be ordered when vasculitis/ ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              glomerulonephritis is in the differential diagnosis.  "UC-ANCA" is the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              test to order to evaluate patients with suspected inflammatory bowel or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              liver disease \(see UC-ANCA listing for more testing information\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The "ANCA" test starts with immunofluorescence screening for both ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              C-ANCA \(primarily associated with Wegner's granulomatosis\) and p-ANCA ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(primarily associated with microscopic polyarteritis and pauci-immune ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              GN\). If the ANCA screen is positive, titration to end-point is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              performed. It is strongly recommended that confirmatory testing for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              anti-proteinase 3 \(PR3\) and anti-myeloperoxidase \(MPO\) be performed ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              at the time of initial identification of ANCA. P-ANCA can be confused ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with "UC-ANCA" or ANA on IFA screening.  Approximately 5% of patients ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with either "C-ANCA" or "P-ANCA" will have a specificity different from ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              that usually associated with the ANCA IFA pattern \(eg: P-ANCA may have ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              PR3 specificity and the C-ANCA may have MPO specificity\).</pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                        See:  <br />Myeloperoxidase Antibodies, IgG, Serum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br />Proteinase 3 Antibodies, IgG, Serum ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br />UC-ANCA Screen and Interpretation, Serum  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ANCA screen and titer:  Indirect Immunofluorescence ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              MPO and PR3:  Multiplex flow immunoassay</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  3 days  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(            Testing Schedule  Daily - Batch analysis performed daily excluding  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              weekends and university holidays.  ) Tj
/F00 8 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
() Tj
/F01 8 Tf
0.0000 Tw
(Neutrophil Oxidative Burst \(DHR\)) Tj
/F00 8 Tf
0.0000 Tw
( ) Tj
/F10 8 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                  Laboratory  VA Diagnostic Immunology Lab  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  10 mL; sodium heparin green top.  Do not use a needle smaller than 21 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              gauge.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  Internal control and normal range reported with each sample.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  This assay is run using viable lymphocytes.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              This assay is used to determine whether the NADPH Oxidase of phagocytic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cells in a certain individual is normal.  This is done by flow ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cytometry using the probe dihydrorhodamine 123 \(DHR\).  This assay ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              replaces the Nitro Blue Tetrazolium test \(NBT\).  This assay is the gold ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              standard to rule out Chronic Granulomatous disease \(CGD\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(            Testing Schedule  This assay is run Monday through Thursday during working hours and  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 78.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Friday 8 a.m. to noon.  ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
