(                              Beginning October 1, 2009, the "Lipid Panel" orderable within Epic will ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              include a calculation for non-high density lipoprotein \(non-HDL-C\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Non-HDL-C is calculated as total cholesterol minus HDL. The addition of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              non-HDL-C to the Lipid Panel reflects the recognition of this ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              calculated value as a predictive factor in cardiovascular disease based ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              on the National Cholesterol Education III studies. The reference ranges ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              for non-HDL-C are based on National Cholesterol Education III ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              guidelines: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                  Desirable:          < 130 mg/dL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                  Borderline high:    139-159 mg/dL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                  High:               160-189 mg/dL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                  Very high:          > or = 190 mg/dL ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Because non-HDL-C is simply a calculated parameter, there are no ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              changes to the sample requirements for the "Lipid Panel".</pre> ) Tj
