(                    Comments  Abnormal oxygen-affinity is demonstrated in the presence of some ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hemoglobin variants:<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -High oxygen-affinity causes erythrocytosis<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              -Low oxygen-affinity causes cyanosis<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Increased oxygen-affinity of hemoglobin, reflected in a low p50, left- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              shifted oxygen dissociation curve, and loss of normal sigmoidal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              configuration, is characteristic of many hemoglobin variants that are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              responsible for polycythemia. Measurement of oxygen-affinity is the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              most important method for diagnosis of these disorders.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <u>Cautions</u>:  To ensure valid results, the specimen must be < or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              =72 hours old. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                See Appendix  See Additional Information: <br /> ) Tj
