0.0000 Tw
(                              </table> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  Adult or pediatric: 10 mL; yellow top tube \(ACD-A\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  An interpretative report will be provided by the pathologist.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Immunopathology or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Ham's acid hemolysin and sucrose lysis tests have been replaced by flow ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              cytometric testing for glycosylphosphatidyl inositol \(GPI\)-anchored ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              proteins CD14 and CD24, and aerolysin binding. These proteins are not ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              expressed on PNH white blood cells and their lack of expression is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              determined by flow cytometric assay. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The channel-forming toxin, aerolysin, and its inactive precursors, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              proaerolysin, bind selectively with a high affinity to the GPI anchor ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              itself. The lack of CPI anchor on blood cell surface will decrease the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ability of fluorescently labeled protein aerolysin \(FLAER\) to bind to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              nucleated blood cells in patients with PNH. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria \(PNH\) is a stem cell disorder in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              which the affected cells are deficient in GPI-anchored proteins. GPI- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              anchored proteins include a number of important molecules on the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              surfaces of blood cells of all lineages. These include CD14 on ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              monocytes and CD24 on granulocytes. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Determination of CD14 and CD24 must be performed on fresh whole blood. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Both monocytes and granulocytes are analyzed for CD14/CD24 expression ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and aerolysin bindings. Granulocytes are the most sensitive population ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in which to detect GPI-anchored protein deficiency. Two additional ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              markers are performed for gating purposes, CD45 \(leukocyte common ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              antigen\) and CD15 \(myeloid antigen\). ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Results are issued as a Bone Marrow \(H-6\) report interpreted by a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              pathologist. The number of GPI-anchored protein deficient cells can ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              vary widely from case to case. Those patients with the highest relative ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              numbers of GPI-anchored protein deficient cells are most likely to have ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              classical PNH symptoms, while those with small relative numbers are ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              more likely to present with aplastic anemia or myelodysplastic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              syndrome. About 20-25% of patients with aplastic anemia and MDS have ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              been found to demonstrate small clones of PNH cells, so studies for PNH ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              may also be indicted in patients with these diagnoses. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              REFS: ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              1\)Richards, S et al. Application of Flow Cytometry to the Diagnosis of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Paroxysmal Noctural Hemoglobinuria. Cytometry 2000; 42:223-233. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              2\)Dunn, D, et al. Paroxysmal Nocturnal Hemoglobinuria in Patients with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Bone Marrow Failure Syndromes. Ann Int Med 1999; 131:401-408. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              3\) Brodsky RA, et al. Improved detection and characterization of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria using fluorescent aerolysin. Am J ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Clin Pathol 2000; 114:459-66. </pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                See Appendix  See Additional Information: <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Specimens Requiring Immediate Delivery  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Flow Cytometry  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
