( Alternate Collection Media:  Call laboratory for additional acceptable specimen collection containers.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  3 mL whole blood in light green top tube or TWO microtainers.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  No accepted reference range.  There is an increased probability of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              prostate cancer with lower %FPSA.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a General Lab or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  <pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Prostate-specific antigen \(PSA\) is a glycoprotein \(molecular weight ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              30,000-34,000 daltons\) having a close structural relationship to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              glandular kallikrein. It has the function of a serine protease. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The proteolytic activity of PSA in blood is inhibited by the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              irreversible formation of complexes with proteinase inhibitors such as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              alpha-1-antichymotrypsin, alpha-2-macroglobulin and other acute phase ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              proteins. In addition to being present in these complexes, PSA is also ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              present in blood in the free form, but is proteolytically inactive. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              PSA tests lack sufficient sensitivity and specificity to be considered ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ideal or absolutely diagnostic for screening or early detection because ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              PSA is not specific for prostate cancer. PSA is organ specific, being ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              produced primarily by prostatic secretory epithelium, but has long been ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              known to be elevated in non-malignant conditions such as benign ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              prostatic hyperplasia \(BPH\). A number of studies have found that the % ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              free PSA was significantly lower in patients having prostate cancer ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              than those with benign disease or normal controls. The ratio fPSA/tPSA ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              has been demonstrated to improve the sensitivity and specificity in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              patients with tPSA values in the "gray zone" of 4-10 ng/mL. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              An equimolar tPSA determination is the prerequisite for reliable ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ratios. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              In patients receiving therapy, particularly hormone withdrawal therapy, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the fPSA/tPSA ratio cannot be utilized to differentiate prostate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              hyperplasia from cancer of the prostate. Combining tests from different ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              manufacturers to determine tPSA and fPSA can produce erroneous values, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              since total PSA tests may be standardized by differing methods or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              detect free PSA to differing degrees. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The free PSA immunoassay is indicated for measurement of fPSA in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              conjunction with the total PSA assay to develop a ratio of fPSA to tPSA ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(%fPSA\). This ratio is useful when used in conjunction with the Total ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              PSA test as an aid in distinguishing prostate cancer from benign ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              prostatic conditions in men age 50 years or older who have a digital ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              rectal examination \(DRE\) that is not suspicious for prostate cancer and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              an total PSA value in the range 4-10 ng/mL. Prostate biopsy is required ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              for the diagnosis of prostate cancer. </pre> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Electrochemiluminescence Immunoassay  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  1 hour \(upon receipt in laboratory\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(            Testing Schedule  24 hrs/day, 7 days a week, including holidays.  ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(602) Tj
