(                              plasma cell dyscrasia by electrophoresis, but are detectable when ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 746.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              present as M-proteins.  Polyclonal IgA can be seen in cirrhosis. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 722.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Radiocontrast dyes used in imaging can produce small peaks by capillary ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 710.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              electrophoresis.  Iohexol and iopamidol show up in the alpha-2 region. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 698.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              It is recommended to delay electrophoresis, if possible, for several ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 686.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              days after radiocontrast dye administration. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 662.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Gelatin-based plasma substitutes can produce polyclonal-like increases ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 650.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in beta-gamma and gamma regions. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Piperacillin-tazobactam can produce a small peak in the beta-1 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 614.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              region.</pre> ) Tj
