1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Useful for investigating possible disorders of mitochondrial ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              metabolism, when used in conjunction with cerebrospinal fluid lactate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              collected at the same time to determine the lactate-to-pyruvate ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ratio.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Evaluating patients with neurologic dysfunction and normal blood ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              lactate-to-pyruvate ratios.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pyruvic acid, an intermediate metabolite, plays an important role in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              linking carbohydrate and amino acid metabolism to the tricarboxylic ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              acid cycle, the fatty acid beta-oxidation pathway, and the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mitochondrial respiratory chain complex. Though pyruvate is not ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              diagnostic in itself, analysis with lactate has diagnostic value as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              many inborn errors of metabolism present with laboratory findings that ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              include lactic acidosis and/or a high lactate:pyruvate \(L:P\) ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              ratio.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The L:P ratio is elevated in several, but not all, mitochondrial ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              respiratory chain disorders. Determination of lactate, pyruvate, and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              L:P ratio in cerebrospinal fluid is helpful in directing attention ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              toward a possible mitochondrial disorder in cases with predominantly ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              neurologic dysfunction and normal blood lactate levels.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <strong><u>Cautions</u>:</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Correct specimen collection and handling is crucial to achieve reliable ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              results.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Pyruvic acid levels alone have little clinical utility. Abnormal ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              concentrations of pyruvic acid, and lactate-to-pyruvate \(L:P\) ratios, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              are not diagnostic for a particular disorder but must be interpreted in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              the context of the patient's clinical presentation and other laboratory ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              studies.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              For the L:P ratio, both analytes should be determined on the same ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              specimen.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              When comparing blood and cerebrospinal fluid \(CSF\) L:P ratios, blood ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              and CSF specimens should be collected at the same time. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                        See:  <br />Pyruvic Acid, Blood  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Spectrophotometry \(SP\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  4 working days upon receipt at reference laboratory  ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(Updated:Mon Aug 26 14:13:27 2013) Tj
