(                              10 IU/mL or greater: Positive - IgG antibody to rubella detected, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                                              which may indicate a current or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                                              previous exposure/immunization to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                                                              rubella. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Rubella IgG antibody can be formed following rubella infection or after ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              rubella vaccination.  A reactive result is consistent with immune ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              status to rubella virus.  Non-reactive and equivocal results flag as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              abnormal in Epic which indicates non-immune or equivocal immune status ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              to rubella.  A non-reactive result does NOT imply rubella infection. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              If ordered in workup of possible rubella infection, the IgG antibody ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              results should be interpreted in conjunction with other laboratory ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              tests, clinical history, and physical examination.</pre>  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
