0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <strong><u>Cautions</u>:</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Reference ranges were derived using fasting specimens from healthy ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              individuals. Sitosterol and campesterol values may be mildly elevated ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              in individuals whose diets include foods with high concentrations of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              plant sterols, such as some vegetable oils and infant formulas.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a Miscellaneous Request or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Please print, complete and submit the <a ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              href="http://www.mayomedicallaboratories.com/it- ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mmfiles/InformedConsent.pdf">Informed Consent for Genetic Testing</a> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              to the lab, with the specimen and the A-1a Miscellaneous Request or ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Epic Req.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Testing includes desmosterol, lathosterol, campesterol, and sitosterol ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              for the investigation of desmosterolosis and sitosterolemia.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <strong><u>Clinical Information</u>:</strong><br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Cholesterol plays an essential role in many cellular and developmental ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              processes. In addition to its role as a membrane lipid, it is the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              precursor to numerous molecules that play an important role in cell ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              growth and differentiation, protein glycosylation, and signaling ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              pathways. The biosynthesis of cholesterol and its subsequent conversion ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              to other essential compounds is complex, involving a number of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              intermediates and enzymes. Disorders that result from a deficiency of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              these enzymes lead to an accumulation of specific intermediates and ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              inhibit the formation of important biomolecules. Clinical findings ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              common to cholesterol biosynthesis disorders include congenital ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              skeletal malformations, dysmorphic facial features, psychomotor ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              retardation, and failure to thrive. One example is desmosterolosis ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              \(desmosterol reductase deficiency\), which has a similar phenotype to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Smith-Lemli-Opitz \(SLO\) syndrome \(7-dehydrocholesterol reductase ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 203.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              deficiency\). Its biochemical marker is the elevation of desmosterol in ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              plasma, tissue, and cultured cells.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Sitosterolemia is a rare autosomal recessive disorder caused by ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              mutations in 2 ATP-binding cassette \(ABC\) transporter genes, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 155.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <em>ABCG5</em> and <em>ABCG8</em>, which abnormally enhance the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 146.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              absorption of plant sterols and cholesterol from the intestines. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 136.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Patients often present with tendon and tuberous xanthomas as well as ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 126.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              premature coronary artery disease. A biochemical diagnosis of ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 117.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              sitosterolemia is made by documenting elevations of the plant sterols ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 107.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              sitosterol and campesterol in plasma or serum. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 88.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                See Appendix  See Additional Information: <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 78.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Fasting Specimen Requirements  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 69.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry \(GC-MS\)/Gas Chromatography-Flame ) Tj
