( Alternate Collection Media:  Call laboratory for additional acceptable specimen collection containers.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 645.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                     Minimum  3.0 mL whole blood from red top tube or TWO microtainers.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 635.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(             Reference Range  Reference range and methodology changed effective 12/11/2012.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 626.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 616.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              9 IU/mL or less: Negative - No significant level of detectable ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 606.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Toxoplasma gondii IgG antibody.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 597.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 587.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              10-11 IU/mL: Equivocal - Repeat testing in 10-14 days may be ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 578.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              helpful.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 568.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 558.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              12 IU/mL or greater: Positive - IgG antibody to Toxoplasma detected, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 549.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              which may indicate a current or past Toxoplasma infection.  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 539.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Order Form:  A-1a General Lab or Epic Req  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 530.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                    Comments  Acute and convalescent specimens must be labeled as such; parallel ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 520.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              testing is preferred and convalescent specimens must be received within ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 510.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              30 days from receipt of the acute specimens. Please mark specimen ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 501.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              plainly as "ACUTE" or "CONVALESCENT."<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 491.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 482.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Toxoplasmosis is an infection caused by the parasite Toxoplasma gondii. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The infection is mainly acquired by ingestion of food or water that is ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 462.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              contaminated by mature oocysts shed by cats or by undercooked meat ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 453.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              containing tissue cysts.  Primary acute infection occurs in many ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 443.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              individuals and usually produces mild symptoms followed by a latent ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 434.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              period that may persist for life.  However, reactivation of a latent ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Toxoplasma infection as a result of immunosuppression can lead to ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 414.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              meningoencephalitis.<br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 405.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              <br /> ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 395.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              Primary maternal Toxoplasma infection occurring during pregnancy can ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 386.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              lead to severe damage of the fetus as the parasite can be transmitted ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              across the placenta. Infants with congenital infection often do not ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 366.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              present with clinical symptoms at birth but may develop severe sequelae ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 357.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              later in life such as mental and psychomotor retardation, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 347.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              chorioretinitis and hearing loss. The fetal infection rate increases ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 338.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              with gestational age at which the mother acquires Toxoplasma infection. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              However, the risk of severe clinical manifestations is higher in case ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 318.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              of early maternal infection.  Early drug therapy in acute infection ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 309.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              during pregnancy can prevent congenital damage or ameliorate the ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 299.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              severity of clinical manifestations.  The diagnosis of Toxoplasma ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 290.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              infection is most commonly made by the detection of IgG and IgM ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              antibodies directed against Toxoplasma. The determination of IgG ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 270.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              antibodies to Toxoplasma gondii is used to assess the serological ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 261.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              status to T. gondii and is indicative of an acute or latent infection. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 251.6 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              The detection of IgM antibodies to T. gondii indicates an acute, recent ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 242.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              or reactivated Toxoplasma infection.  The diagnosis of the acute ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 232.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              acquired infection during pregnancy is established by a seroconversion ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 222.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              or a significant rise in antibody titers \(IgG and/or IgM\) in serial ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 213.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                              samples. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 194.0 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                        See:  <br />Toxoplasmosis Antibody, IgM, Serum  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 184.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(                 Methodology  Multiplex Flow Immunoassay  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 174.8 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(               Analytic Time  3 hours \(upon receipt in laboratory\)  ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 165.2 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(            Testing Schedule  24 hrs/day, 7 days a week, including holidays.  ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72 37 Tm
(Updated:Mon Aug 26 14:13:27 2013) Tj
